    ('layerzero:ZRO', 'https://docs.google.com/document/d/1gDZRoDDQUiW0-tm-JPuPXVgC8QrVA0huT7MIqhJ-__0/edit', $tank_seed_ZRO_20261110$## ZRO — LayerZero: token & protocol fact sheet

As of 2026-11-10

### Executive summary

ZRO is the fixed-supply (1,000,000,000) governance and value-capture token of LayerZero, the cross-chain messaging protocol behind the OFT token standard used by USDT0, PYUSD, USDe, USDG, WBTC and many other assets. Today the only recurring value that reaches holders is a monthly open-market ZRO buyback funded by revenue from Stargate, the bridge app LayerZero bought in August 2025. These buybacks totalled 2,721,665 ZRO for a cost of $3.98M since September 2025. The last three months ran at about $3.4M a year, which is about 0.6% of market cap ($596.6M on 2026-11-10, CoinGecko). Tokens sit in a Foundation wallet. They are not burned. The protocol-level fee switch, which would add a fee on every message and burn ZRO, has failed four votes on low turnout. Messaging fees (about $2.3M over the last 12 months per DefiLlama) go to DVNs and Executors, which are mostly LayerZero Labs businesses, and not to the token.

The market prices ZRO mainly on the future Zero L1 blockchain and ATLAS exchange engine. ZRO would be gas, staking collateral and the burn target there. Zero has institutional partners (Citadel Securities, DTCC, ICE, Tether, Google Cloud, ARK) but no public mainnet date. The current state is mixed. Adoption is strong, but the KelpDAO exploit on April 18, 2026 ($292M lost through a 1-of-1 LayerZero Labs DVN setup) damaged trust. Stargate revenue is far below its $100M-ARR 2026 goal. Investor unlocks (about 12.7M ZRO a month gross to strategic partners until about mid-2027) continue. The most important thing to watch: the Zero mainnet date. It turns on ZRO gas, staking and burn demand, and it also re-releases the 183M ZRO of Foundation tokens that are locked "until Zero mainnet".

### What the token is

- Ticker / name: ZRO / "LayerZero" (on-chain symbol() = ZRO, name() = LayerZero, 18 decimals). Verified contract name on Etherscan: LayerZeroToken (Solidity 0.8.22). It is an OFT (Omnichain Fungible Token): it burns on the source chain and mints on the destination chain through the LayerZero V2 endpoint (endpoint() on Ethereum returns 0x1a44076050125825900e736c501f859c50fe728c).

- Contract address (same on all EVM chains): 0x6985884c4392d348587b19cb9eaaf157f13271cd. Ethereum, Arbitrum, Optimism, Base, BNB Chain, Polygon and Avalanche are listed by [CoinGecko](https://api.coingecko.com/api/v3/coins/layerzero).

- Owner/admin: On Ethereum, owner() = 0xcda8e3add00c95e5035617f970096118ca2f4c92, a Gnosis Safe with getThreshold() = 3 of 5 owners (getOwners()), read on-chain on 2026-11-10. LayerZero said on 2026-11-03 that ZRO contract ownership "is being migrated to OneSig" (its own multisig) ahead of Zero mainnet, and that ZRO's DVN config will move to 4-of-4 required DVNs ([source](https://layerzero.network/blog/ecosystem-update-november-2026)).

- Launch: TGE and airdrop claim on June 20, 2024 ([Introducing ZRO](https://info.layerzero.foundation/introducing-zro-d39df554a9b7)).

