### Revenue and value capture

#### (a) Gross fees paid by users

- Messaging fees (DVN + Executor, paid in native gas): $16,190 (24h, 2026-11-09), $91,684 (7d), $390,675 (30d), $2,334,013 (1y), $76.56M all-time (DefiLlama, from ExecutorFeePaid and DVNFeePaid events on SendUln302/SendUln301). Monthly: Sept 2026 $289K, Oct 2026 $372K (the highest month in 12). This followed the LayerZero Labs Executor minimum fee rising to $0.25 per transaction from Sept 1, 2026 ([pricing update](https://layerzero.network/blog/pricing-updates)).

- Stargate fees: $280,307 (30d) and $2,265,793 (1y) per DefiLlama. From Sept 1, 2026, Stargate OFT transfers carry a product fee of up to 2 bps, capped at $250 per transfer.

#### (b) Protocol revenue

- LayerZero protocol take rate = 0%. The fee switch is off. About 100% of messaging fees go to DVNs and Executors, a large but undisclosed share of them to LayerZero Labs. Labs' revenue is private.

- Stargate revenue (owned by the Foundation): the Foundation says Sept–Nov 2025 revenue was $2.4M, of which $1.2M bought ZRO ([Dec 1, 2025](https://layerzero.network/blog/understanding-zro-buybacks)). The stated goal was "$100M ARR in 2026". The implied actual run-rate from April–October 2026 buybacks (100% of Stargate revenue since April, per LayerZero) is about $1.47M over 7 months, or about $2.5M a year. That is about 2.5% of the target (estimate).

