Mechanism: Purchases are executed off-chain or through an exchange/OTC desk, then withdrawn to the Foundation buyback wallet 0x6ac55e733dff03a54251670df0667774e8f7d28f, a OneSig contract on Ethereum. The sending addresses rotate (for example 0x2e1078…, 0xccb733…, 0x79e2b9…, 0x18b3bf…, 0xe6e96c…, 0x6fbb43…, 0xcd531a…). The latest sender, 0xcd531ae9… (active since March 2021), moved about $69.9M USDC and $39.4M USDT across its latest 200 token transfers in about 9 hours on 2026-11-10 (Etherscan tokentx). That pattern looks like an exchange or custodian hot wallet; there is no public label. No burn function is called. The ZRO sits in the Foundation wallet, so holders benefit only through lower float, and the Foundation could redeploy the tokens. The 50% revenue share with former veSTG holders ended in March 2026. Since April 2026, 100% of Stargate revenue has gone to buybacks (The ZRO Token, 2026-06-03).

Other "buybacks" (one-off, not recurring holder revenue): Foundation bought 50M ZRO from strategic partners in Sept 2025 (OTC, price not disclosed). Labs made a $10M open-market purchase in Nov 2025. LayerZero counts $112.7M deployed into ZRO buybacks since Sept 2025 across all entities (company figure, June 2026).

Source disagreement: DefiLlama's layerzero HoldersRevenue reads $0 for 24h/7d/30d. Its 1y figure ($3.39M) has no entries for Oct and Nov 2026, even though receipts on 2026-10-06 and 2026-11-05 are visible on-chain. This is a DefiLlama indexing gap. Separately, DefiLlama Stargate revenue is lower than the Foundation's figures before March 2026 (Sept–Nov 2025: DefiLlama Stargate fees $611K vs the Foundation's $2.4M of Stargate revenue). The likely reason is that DefiLlama misses LZ Assets and Hydra fee lines. For Apr–Oct 2026 the two sources are closer: DefiLlama monthly Stargate fees vs the Foundation buyback cost differ by -18% to +30% per month (for example Sep 2026: $458K vs $352K; May 2026: $117K vs $143K).

#### Monetization plan (what is not live)

- Protocol fee switch: Votes are held every 6 months. Results: Dec 2024 (turnout 10.96%), Jun 2025 (13.01%), Dec 2025 (3.71%), Jun 20–27, 2026 (3,519,727 ZRO voted: 3,408,922 for vs 110,806 against. That is 2.82% of the 124,448,943-ZRO quorum, or about 0.87% turnout of the 403.4M eligible supply). All four were "Off", each with more than 96% Yes but no quorum. Next expected window: about Dec 20–27, 2026 (6-month cadence; not yet announced as of 2026-11-10). [Fee switch page](https://layerzero.foundation/fee-switch).

- Labs discretionary buys: "will scale with Labs profitability", with no fixed cadence.

- Zero/ATLAS: gas, staking, and buy-and-burn of 75% of post-rebate ATLAS fees, plus Zero network fees, priority fees and MEV through buyback and burn. Not live, and no date.

### How to verify on-chain

All values below were first obtained on 2026-11-10 at about 15:15–15:25 UTC (Ethereum block about 26,385,353). The fact-checker re-ran commands 1–7 at about 16:00–16:10 UTC (Ethereum block 26,385,592) and got identical on-chain results (supply, balance, owner, threshold, vote result); only market data moved. Replace $ETHERSCAN_API_KEY with your own key.

#### 1. Total supply per chain (should sum to 1,000,000,000)

for rpc in ethereum-rpc arbitrum-one-rpc optimism-rpc base-rpc bsc-rpc polygon-bor-rpc avalanche-c-chain-rpc; do  curl -s -X POST https://$rpc.publicnode.com -H 'content-type: application/json' \   -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"eth_call","params":[{"to":"0x6985884c4392d348587b19cb9eaaf157f13271cd","data":"0x18160ddd"},"latest"]}'; echo " $rpc"; done# Ethereum result 0x...0312b7d20580ab0e2e2a0000 = 951,083,761.50 ZRO

#### 2. Buyback wallet balance (Foundation, Stargate-funded)

curl -s -X POST https://ethereum-rpc.publicnode.com -H 'content-type: application/json' \ -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"eth_call","params":[{"to":"0x6985884c4392d348587b19cb9eaaf157f13271cd","data":"0x70a082310000000000000000000000006ac55e733dff03a54251670df0667774e8f7d28f"},"latest"]}'# result 0x...02405c047e9cf1da0301dc = 2,721,780.52 ZRO

#### 3. Every buyback receipt (ZRO Transfer events into the wallet)

curl -s "https://api.etherscan.io/v2/api?chainid=1&module=account&action=tokentx&contractaddress=0x6985884c4392d348587b19cb9eaaf157f13271cd&address=0x6ac55e733dff03a54251670df0667774e8f7d28f&sort=asc&apikey=$ETHERSCAN_API_KEY"# 20 transfers; latest 2026-11-05 23:19 UTC, 183,874.87 ZRO from 0xcd531ae9efcce479654c4926dec5f6209531ca7b

Compare the result with the Foundation's table at [layerzero.foundation/zro-buybacks](https://layerzero.foundation/zro-buybacks) (2,721,665 ZRO and $3,980,541 cost basis on 2026-11-10). A burn would show as a Transfer to 0x0 or a drop in totalSupply. Neither has happened.

#### 4. Fee-switch vote result

curl -s https://layerzero.foundation/api/proposal-info# {"state":3,"quorum":"124448943190000000000000000","quorumPercentageReached":2.82,#  "forVotes":"3408921764911663313006649","againstVotes":"110805674718814392621201","finalized":true}

Cross-check on-chain (re-run 2026-11-10). The vote #4 governor on Arbitrum is 0x9006d631fc6fc7d454abedec9157db1ae81b73b9 (LzFeeSwitchGovernorMain, OpenZeppelin Governor with a timestamp clock). The address 0xB958…C637 is not the governor: it is the LayerzeroFeeSwitch flag contract that the governor toggles.

# state(proposalId) -> 3 (Defeated); proposalVotes(proposalId) -> against 110,805.67 / for 3,408,921.76 / abstain 0PID=53686114529839349371587229767547771257939000879400110908539992016013405972287PH=$(python3 -c "print(hex($PID)[2:].zfill(64))")curl -s -X POST https://arbitrum-one-rpc.publicnode.com -H 'content-type: application/json' \ -d "{\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":1,\"method\":\"eth_call\",\"params\":[{\"to\":\"0x9006d631fc6fc7d454abedec9157db1ae81b73b9\",\"data\":\"0x3e4f49e6$PH\"},\"latest\"]}"# 0x544ffc9c = proposalVotes(uint256); 0xf8ce560a = quorum(uint256) with timepoint 1781913600 (2026-06-20 00:00 UTC) -> 124,448,943.19 ZRO# feeSwitch() on the flag contract -> falsecurl -s -X POST https://arbitrum-one-rpc.publicnode.com -H 'content-type: application/json' \ -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"eth_call","params":[{"to":"0xB9582701a5cB61FDe46EF0eea816D404A8FFc637","data":"0x88916b5b"},"latest"]}'

#### 5. Messaging fees and Stargate revenue (DefiLlama)

curl -s "https://api.llama.fi/summary/fees/layerzero?dataType=dailyFees"          # total30d 390,675curl -s "https://api.llama.fi/summary/fees/layerzero?dataType=dailyHoldersRevenue" # buyback receipts (gap for Oct-Nov 2026)curl -s "https://api.llama.fi/summary/fees/stargate-finance?dataType=dailyRevenue" # total30d 280,307curl -s "https://api.llama.fi/protocol/stargate-finance"                           # TVL 83.9M

To recompute messaging fees yourself, sum ExecutorFeePaid(address,uint256) and DVNFeePaid(address[],address[],uint256[]) logs on the SendUln302 send library. On Ethereum the send libraries are 0xbB2Ea70C9E858123480642Cf96acbcCE1372dCe1 (ULN302) and 0xD231084BfB234C107D3eE2b22F97F3346fDAF705 (ULN301). The full list is in the [DefiLlama adapter](https://github.com/DefiLlama/dimension-adapters/blob/master/fees/layerzero.ts).

#### 6. Admin / ownership

# ZRO owner() on Ethereum -> 0xcda8e3add00c95e5035617f970096118ca2f4c92 (Gnosis Safe)curl -s -X POST https://ethereum-rpc.publicnode.com -H 'content-type: application/json' \ -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"eth_call","params":[{"to":"0x6985884c4392d348587b19cb9eaaf157f13271cd","data":"0x8da5cb5b"},"latest"]}'# getThreshold() on the Safe -> 3curl -s -X POST https://ethereum-rpc.publicnode.com -H 'content-type: application/json' \ -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"eth_call","params":[{"to":"0xcda8e3add00c95e5035617f970096118ca2f4c92","data":"0xe75235b8"},"latest"]}'

Watch for a change of owner() to a OneSig contract, as announced on 2026-11-03.

#### 7. Live message flow and market data

curl -s "https://scan.layerzero-api.com/v1/messages/latest?limit=5"   # latest cross-chain messages (e.g. USDT0 Ethereum->Celo)curl -s -X POST https://api.hyperliquid.xyz/info -H 'content-type: application/json' -d '{"type":"metaAndAssetCtxs"}'  # ZRO OI 28.45M at 16:09 UTC (28.48M at 15:17 UTC)curl -s "https://fapi.binance.com/fapi/v1/openInterest?symbol=ZROUSDT"   # 18.03M ZRO at 16:09 UTC (18.07M at 15:17 UTC)

### Key people

- Bryan Pellegrino — Co-founder and CEO, LayerZero Labs. Confirmed in the Nov 4, 2026 press release. X: [@PrimordialAA](https://x.com/PrimordialAA). He is the public face of Zero, ATLAS and the token strategy.

- Ryan Zarick — Co-founder and CTO (protocol and engineering). X: @ryanzarick. The X handle and current role come from public records and were not re-verified in this research. No official LayerZero page fetched on 2026-11-10 lists the executive team.

- Caleb Banister — Co-founder. Based on public records; his current role was not re-verified.

- Structure: LayerZero Labs (private company, Vancouver) builds the protocol, Zero and ATLAS, and runs the Executor, the LayerZero Labs DVN and commercial products. The LayerZero Foundation (X: [@LayerZero_Fndn](https://x.com/LayerZero_Fndn)) holds the community allocation, runs governance (fee-switch referendums), owns and operates Stargate since August 2025, and runs the buybacks. There is no on-chain DAO treasury governance beyond the fee-switch vote. Official accounts: [@LayerZero_Core](https://x.com/LayerZero_Core), @StargateFinance.

- Advisors and strategic investors (June 2026): Cathie Wood (ARK) and Michael Blaugrund (ICE, VP Strategic Initiatives) joined the LayerZero advisory board. Strategic ZRO and equity investors include a16z crypto (lead investor since Series A+), Citadel Securities, ARK Invest and Tether.

- Departures and personnel events: No executive departures were found in the official sources reviewed. LayerZero disclosed (May 8, 2026) that "one of the signers on our multisig" had used the multisig hardware wallet for a personal trade about 3.5 years earlier. That signer was removed and wallets were rotated.

