- 2026-08-25 — ATLAS launched as a concept and product: a headless exchange on Zero with 75% of post-rebate fees going to buy and burn ZRO ([link](https://layerzero.network/blog/introducing-atlas)).

- 2026-08-07 — V1 default library moved to ULN301 (minimum 3-of-3). LayerZero Labs V1 Relayer deprecation set for Dec 15, 2026 ([link](https://layerzero.network/blog/ongoing-security-updates-3)).

Earlier context: Fee switch vote #4 failed (Jun 20–27, 2026). "The ZRO Token" supply and value-capture post (Jun 3, 2026). KelpDAO incident report (May 20), apology (May 8) and exploit (Apr 18, 2026). Zero announced (Feb 10, 2026). Stargate acquisition approved by STG holders (vote Aug 17–24, 2025: 7.22M For vs 0.40M Against, at 0.08634 ZRO per STG).

Research limit: the web-search quota was exhausted early in this run. News was compiled from LayerZero's and the Foundation's own publications, governance and on-chain data. Third-party coverage of legal actions, such as litigation after KelpDAO, was not checked.

### Current problems and risks

- KelpDAO exploit and trust damage. On 2026-04-18, 116,500 rsETH (about $292M) was stolen. Attackers attributed to DPRK's TraderTraitor/UNC4899 (per Mandiant and CrowdStrike) socially engineered a LayerZero Labs developer (breach began 2026-03-06), poisoned two internal RPC nodes, and DDoSed the external RPC. As a result, the LayerZero Labs DVN signed a forged message. KelpDAO used a 1-of-1 DVN setup. The immutable protocol worked as designed, but the operator Labs controls was the single point of failure. LayerZero first blamed KelpDAO's config and then apologized ("we made a mistake by allowing our DVN to act as a 1/1 DVN"). Price fell from about $1.99 (Apr 14) to $0.82 (Jun 9) and $0.75 (Jun 28) (DefiLlama daily). Sources: [statement](https://layerzero.network/blog/kelpdao-incident-statement), [apology](https://layerzero.network/blog/an-overdue-apology), [report](https://layerzero.network/blog/layerzero-labs-kelpdao-incident-report).

- Centralization of defaults and admin. The Labs multisig controls Endpoint defaults, and many apps use defaults. ZRO's own Ethereum owner is a 3-of-5 Gnosis Safe. The multisig-signer personal-trade disclosure adds to this. Hardening is in progress (OneSig 5/7 moving to 7/10, minimum 3-of-3 defaults, Rust "Veritas" second client).

- Weak value accrual today. Holder value is about $3.4M a year (about 0.6% of market cap), and the tokens are not burned. The fee switch failed four times; the last vote reached only 2.82% of quorum (about 0.87% turnout of eligible supply). Holders have shown little interest in voting, and the dynamic-quorum floor is still 20%.

- Stargate is shrinking. TVL fell from $240M to $84M year over year (-65%). Revenue runs at about $2.5M a year against the stated $100M-ARR goal for 2026. Bus delivery was discontinued, low-activity chains were dropped, and Stargate v1 was paused and then reopened for redemptions only.

- Unlock overhang. About 12.7M ZRO a month gross to strategic partners until about mid-2027 (plus contributors), and 183M Foundation ZRO tied to the Zero mainnet event.

- Competition. Circle CCTP for native USDC, Chainlink CCIP with banks, Wormhole NTT, and intent-based bridges (Across, deBridge, Relay) take user-facing flow. LayerZero's moat is issuer lock-in to OFT contracts.

- Execution risk on Zero/ATLAS. These are new L1 and exchange products with ambitious performance claims (2M TPS per Zone, 200K TPS demos), and the institutional pilots so far are private-permissioned. There is no public mainnet date. Value capture depends on third-party venues choosing ATLAS.

- Fee pressure on users. The higher Executor minimum ($0.25) and the Stargate bps fee could push price-sensitive flow to competitors.

- What the market believes (bull case): The roughly 3.2x rally from the July 2026 low ($0.707–0.717) to the October high ($2.26–2.27) rests on Zero and ATLAS (TradFi partners DTCC, ICE, Citadel, Tether, Google Cloud), on continued stablecoin-issuer wins (Anchorage/USAT, KRW1, CADC, USDT0 on Stellar), and on the promise that ZRO becomes gas, stake and burn asset for a capital-markets chain. LayerZero's public message is "there is no second token and there never will be."

### What would move the token

| Date | Event | Bullish if | Bearish if |

| --- | --- | --- | --- |

| Around the 20th of each month (Nov 20, Dec 20, 2026 …) | Strategic-partner unlock, about 12.7M ZRO gross | Low exchange inflows | Large deposits to exchanges from investor wallets |

| Early each month (next about early Dec 2026) | Stargate buyback receipt into 0x6ac5…d28f | Rising USD size (the Stargate 2-bps fee is working) | Shrinking size |

| By Dec 15, 2026 | STG→ZRO conversion closes. V1 Relayer and V1 bug bounty end | Conversion overhang ends | Late conversion and selling. Apps stuck on ULNv2 break |

| About Dec 20–27, 2026 (expected, not yet announced) | Fee switch referendum #5 | Quorum met and "Yes", which turns on protocol fees and ZRO burns | Another failure on turnout |

| Not dated (the About page says ATLAS is "launching later this year", i.e. 2026; no Zero mainnet date) | Zero mainnet / ATLAS launch | Mainnet with real venues and volume, ZRO gas and staking live | Delays. Release of the 183M Foundation tokens if demand is not there |

| Ongoing | ZRO ownership migration to OneSig; ZRO DVN 4/4 | Smooth migration | Any incident |

| Ongoing | New issuer and institutional wins; Labs discretionary buybacks | Large issuers (bank stablecoins) launch as OFT; new Labs purchase | Issuer churn to CCTP/CCIP/NTT |

| Until about June 2027 | End of the strategic-partner vesting | Removes a monthly supply source | — |

