### Verification notes

Independent fact-check performed on 2026-11-10 (about 15:55–16:15 UTC) by a second researcher. All reads below were re-run independently; no API keys appear in this document.

#### Re-checked and confirmed

- Supply: totalSupply() on all 7 EVM chains re-read via publicnode RPCs (Ethereum block 26,385,592). Results are identical to the original figures and sum to 1,000,000,000 ZRO. The Ethereum raw hex result in Section 8 matches. CoinGecko circulating 399,976,128 ZRO, total and max 1B: confirmed.

- Contracts: Etherscan V2 getsourcecode confirms ZRO = LayerZeroToken (0.8.22), buyback wallet = OneSig, owner = GnosisSafeProxy. owner(), getThreshold() = 3 and 5 owners from getOwners() re-read on-chain. endpoint() = 0x1a44…728c. Ethereum send libraries 0xbB2E…dCe1 = SendUln302 and 0xD231…F705 = SendUln301.

- Buybacks: the Foundation tracker table (14 monthly rows) re-summed to 2,721,665 ZRO / $3,980,541. TTM $3,131,662 / 2,161,374 ZRO, Aug–Oct $844,726 and Apr–Oct $1,464,835 are all confirmed. Etherscan tokentx shows 20 transfers, and the latest receipts on 2026-10-06 and 2026-11-05 match the doc. The on-chain balance of 2,721,780.52 ZRO equals the net sum of the transfers.

- DefiLlama: LayerZero fees 24h/7d/30d/1y ($16,190 / $91,684 / $390,675 / $2,334,013) and all-time $76.56M; holders revenue $0 for 30d, with the last non-zero day 2026-09-04 and 1y $3,391,192; Stargate fees 30d $280,307 and 1y $2,265,793; Stargate TVL $83.9M (30d ago $109.4M, 1y ago $240.4M); LayerZero "TVL" $16.2B starting 2026-05-02; competitor 30d fees. All confirmed. Note: Stargate 1y revenue on DefiLlama is $1,958,482, below 1y fees.

- Fee switch: proposal-info API re-queried, and the result also confirmed directly on-chain via the Arbitrum governor (state = 3 Defeated; for/against votes; quorum 124,448,943.19 ZRO at timepoint 2026-06-20 00:00 UTC = 30.85% of 403,400,140). Vote dates were checked on the Foundation fee-switch page, and eligibility and abstention terms in the Referendum #4 post (via the Foundation's Medium RSS feed).

- Primary sources: I opened all 50 links in the original document (Medium links return 403 to curl and were read via RSS instead). Publication dates and key facts match the claims: The ZRO Token (514M unlocked, 183M re-locked, 12.7M per month, 134.7M/85.9M, 37.9%, 2.05M per month, $112.7M, 19.77%, 71 DVNs), Understanding ZRO Buybacks, pricing updates, ATLAS (20–65% rebates, 25/75 split, staking up to 1% of supply), 21X (10,000 matches/s, 45x vs L2 EVM baseline, Pellegrino as Co-Founder and CEO), Anchorage, KelpDAO statement and report (116,500 rsETH, about $292M, TraderTraitor/UNC4899, breach from 2026-03-06), the apology, the ecosystem updates of Sep 15, Oct 15 and Nov 3, and the Stellar post (USDT0 >$100B lifetime). The Stargate Snapshot vote was confirmed via GraphQL (7,216,046.5 For / 399,367.8 Against, Aug 17–24, 2025).

#### Corrected

- Wrong contract role. 0xB958…C637 on Arbitrum was described as the referendum/governor contract with quorum()/proposalSnapshot(). It is actually the LayerzeroFeeSwitch on/off flag (feeSwitch() = false). The vote #4 governor is 0x9006d631…73b9. Fixed in Sections 3 and 8 and in the Sources; on-chain verification commands were added.

- Misread pricing post. The Stargate fee is "up to 2 bps, capped at $250 per transfer". Separately, "excess revenue from the fee" funds buybacks. The original text read this as "amounts above the $250 cap go to buybacks". Fixed in Sections 3, 10 and 11.

- Mixed turnout metrics. Vote #4's "2.82%" is the share of quorum reached, not turnout. Actual turnout was about 0.87% of eligible supply (3,519,727 / 403,400,140 ZRO). Clarified alongside the earlier turnout figures (10.96%, 13.01%, 3.71%).

- Buyback reconciliation. The 115.5 ZRO gap between the wallet balance and the Foundation's total is not explained by test transfers (those net to +3 ZRO). It comes mainly from the 2026-02-16 receipt (216,967.26 ZRO vs the 216,852 ZRO booked for Jan 2026).

