As of 2026-11-10. Market data snapshot: CoinGecko API, 2026-11-10 16:08–16:12 UTC (fact-check refresh; original draft 15:20–15:30 UTC). On-chain reads: Ethereum mainnet, blocks ~26,385,381–26,385,6xx (2026-11-10 15:31–16:15 UTC). Research limitation: web-search quota was exhausted in both the drafting and fact-checking sessions; all facts below come from direct fetches of primary pages (Quant RSS feed, Overledger developer docs, GitHub, UK Companies House filings), Ledger Insights articles, CoinGecko/CoinMarketCap/Blockscout/DefiLlama APIs and Etherscan/RPC reads. quant.network HTML pages (including the official QNT token page) returned HTTP 403 (Cloudflare) and could not be read.

### Executive summary

QNT is a 2018 ERC-20 token of Quant with ~14.88m QNT of effective on-chain supply (2026-11-10) and no emission schedule — but supply is not code-capped: the 2018 crowdsale contract that holds the mint right is still controllable by its owner key (0xf5e38b…c4bc, the Quant deployer wallet), and an eth_call simulation on 2026-11-10 shows that key can still record a new "presale purchase" and mint (≥6.47m QNT headroom, more if the sale is re-enabled). Quant is a London-based, privately owned enterprise software company whose product Overledger connects banks and institutions to multiple ledgers. Quant the company is real and profitable — its UK operating entity booked £11.52m revenue and £1.92m pre-tax profit in FY to 30 Sep 2025 — but none of that value reaches QNT holders through any verifiable on-chain mechanism today: the token contract has no burn, fee switch or buyback; the publicly documented mainnet "treasury" contracts were deployed on 2020-06-30 and never used; and 99.8% of the UK entity's revenue is booked as intra-group income from entities under common control, not as QNT flows. The token is in a hype phase: after The Clearing House (TCH) selected Quant on 2026-09-24 to power its US tokenised-deposit "On-Chain Money Initiative", QNT rose from $64.12 (2026-09-21) to $287.38 (2026-10-01, +348%) on up to $1.49bn/day volume, and has since retraced to ~$180.5 (2026-11-10 16:08 UTC, −37% from that peak). The single most important thing to watch is whether Quant's new token utilities — QNT staking against Overledger nodes and QNT as a payment option on its Fusion rollup / Flow Apps, both still in documentation/testnet stage — go live with real, measurable QNT demand, because the bank deals (TCH, GBTD) run on permissioned infrastructure and their public materials do not mention QNT at all.

### What the token is

- Ticker / name: QNT, "Quant". 18 decimals.

- Primary chain: Ethereum. Contract 0x4a220e6096b25eadb88358cb44068a3248254675 (verified source on Etherscan, contract name StandardToken, Solidity v0.4.21). CoinGecko also lists a bridged representation on Energi (0x462b35452e552a66b519ecf70aedb1835d434965) — not issued by Quant itself as far as could be determined.

- Minting: mint() is callable only by the crowdsale address 0x398e41ac3d5972b4bac2320cd130c7a25ca446f7 (a verified Crowdsale contract, Solidity v0.4.21) set at deployment; the token has no cap check of its own. All 608 mint events occurred on 2018-06-25 (10:04–15:26 UTC); no mint has happened since (Etherscan getLogs, re-read 2026-11-10).

- Mint authority is still live (fact-check finding, 2026-11-10): the Crowdsale's owner() is the EOA 0xf5e38bbedc78efea055e0c56035adb320e64c4bc (the wallet that deployed both contracts on 2018-04-06, ran the 2018 distribution, sent the 9.55m QNT to the token contract and funded the 2019 reserve wallets; last outgoing tx 2019-06-08, nonce 817; holds 1.00 QNT). Its owner-only functions recordPresalePurchase(address,uint256) and transferTokensWithOffsetAndLimit(uint256,uint256) have no time or state gate, so the owner can record a new allocation and mint it. Crowdsale state read via eth_call: totalPresaleTokensSold = 8,533,112.51 QNT vs constant cap 15,000,000 → 6,466,887.49 QNT mintable headroom without paying ETH; inSale = false, but enableSale() is owner-only and regularTokenMaxSales − totalRegularTokensSold = 22,466,887.49 − 1,431,146.53 = 21,035,740.97 QNT further headroom (bought at 430 QNT/ETH, with the ETH forwarded to the owner). eth_call simulations from the owner (recordPresalePurchase of 1,000,000 QNT, enableSale()) and of mint() from the crowdsale address all succeed; mint() from any other address reverts. There is no on-chain evidence the key was destroyed or renounced. Quant's "fixed 14.6m max supply" is therefore a policy commitment, not a code guarantee.

- Important quirk: the contract's totalSupply() returns a hard-coded 45,467,000 QNT (the original ICO cap); it is not updated by mint(). Any tool that reads totalSupply() literally will overstate supply by ~3x.

