### The protocol/business

#### What Quant does

Quant Network Ltd (UK company 09798383, incorporated 2015-09-28 as Remitt Ltd, renamed 2017-06-02) is "the principal operating entity of the Quant group … its principal activity is the development of blockchain technology and blockchain-enabled financial infrastructure"; its flagship Overledger "provides financial institutions, central banks, and enterprise clients with a regulated, interoperable gateway to distributed ledger technology" (FY2025 accounts, strategic report). In 2026 the company positions itself as "programmable money infrastructure", focused on tokenised deposits: interbank interoperability/clearing layers, programmable/conditional payments (escrow-style "lock funds", remortgage completions, cross-border, treasury), and TDaaS for banks without their own tokenised-deposit stack.

#### Product lines

- Overledger (Gateway, Connectors, multi-DLT RPC, Overledger Firewall).

- Fusion multi-ledger rollup (+ Trusted Node Program, privacy controls).

- Flow Apps (workflow/orchestration; PayScript language spec repo updated 2026-07-10).

- Tokenised Deposits-as-a-Service (TDaaS).

#### Audience and where it is popular

- Customers: banks, payment-scheme operators, central banks, capital-markets firms. Not a retail/DeFi product; no TVL, no on-chain user base to measure.

- Geography: UK first (GBTD; earlier the UK Regulated Liability Network experiment, where Quant and R3 were selected technology partners in April 2024 with Barclays, Citi, HSBC, Lloyds, NatWest, Nationwide, Santander, Standard Chartered, Virgin Money, Mastercard, Visa; results published September 2024). US via TCH (live target H1 2027). Quant says its technology is deployed "in regulated environments in the UK, Europe and elsewhere". Quant Network Ltd reports "All revenue arose within the United Kingdom" (FY2025).

- Token holder base: retail-heavy, long-dated (196k holders; large share on Binance/Upbit/Kraken/Crypto.com/Bitpanda/Coinspot).

#### Key institutional engagements

