| --- | --- | --- | --- |

| The Clearing House — On-Chain Money Initiative (US) | Interoperability, orchestration and transaction-management layer for clearing/settling tokenised deposits; connectivity to RTP and CHIPS; Quant also the TDaaS provider for TCH-connected banks lacking tokenised-deposit capability | Selected 2026-09-24 after a "competitive process"; network expected available H1 2027. TCH's second track (an L2 blockchain) has no vendor named yet (TCH CEO at Sibos, reported 2026-10-01) | Quant press release & blog; Ledger Insights |

| Great British Tokenised Deposits (GBTD), UK Finance | Platform developer (messaging/interoperability and clearing layer across 7 banks' own tokenised-deposit ledgers; fund-locking) | First live customer transactions reported 2026-09-24 (two remortgage completions); wholesale completions "due shortly" | Ledger Insights 2026-09-24; Quant Sibos recap 2026-10-08 |

| Lloyds Banking Group | Conveyancing/remortgage programmable-payment use case; retail programmable-payment app built "with Quant and Yapily" | Demonstrated at Sibos 2026 | Quant Sibos recap |

| UK Regulated Liability Network (RLN) | Technology partner with R3 | April–September 2024 experiment | Ledger Insights |

