    ('avalanche:AVAX', 'https://docs.google.com/document/d/14EBLBLnI0FHtdm59prFtSzeQHRpTLzPJ3rI0u92Csys/edit', $tank_seed_AVAX_20261110$## AVAX — Avalanche: token & protocol fact sheet

As of 2026-11-10. Market data from CoinGecko at 2026-11-10 16:14 UTC (fact-check refresh); on-chain reads from the public Avalanche RPC (api.avax.network) between 15:23 and 16:20 UTC on 2026-11-10. Values marked "estimate" are derived by the author of this sheet; method is stated next to each.

### Executive summary

AVAX is the native token of Avalanche, a proof-of-stake Layer-1 run by Ava Labs (main developer) and the Avalanche Foundation. AVAX pays gas on the Primary Network (C-Chain, P-Chain, X-Chain), is staked to secure it (2,000 AVAX minimum per validator), and is burned to pay the continuous fee of validators on sovereign Avalanche L1s. The only direct value transfer to holders is the fee burn: every C-Chain fee (base and tip) is burned. That burn is very small: about 37,958 AVAX (about $0.33M) in the last 30 days and 264,524 AVAX (about $2.7M) in the last 12 months. Staking issuance is roughly 10–12M AVAX per year (estimate), so the burn offsets only ~4–5% of it and net supply still grows by roughly 2–2.5% a year. The token is in a deep drawdown: $8.22 on 2026-11-10, down 54% year on year and 94% below its 2021 high. On-chain DeFi has also shrunk (TVL $607M, down 59% y/y; stablecoins $1.26B, down 46% y/y; DefiLlama 2026-11-10). At the same time Avalanche keeps winning institutional deals: NYSE chose it on 2026-11-09 as the core ledger for the clearing firm behind a planned tokenized-securities platform. It also hosts BlackRock BUIDL, and the UAE government uses it. The single most important thing to watch is whether this institutional and L1 adoption starts sending value to AVAX. Two levers matter here. One is the new validator-voted C-Chain fee floor (ACP-283); average daily burn roughly doubled to tripled after the Helicon upgrade (about 640 AVAX/day before vs 1,240–1,720 AVAX/day after). The other is the Foundation's planned capture mechanisms: voluntary revenue sharing and a protocol-owned stablecoin. Today the Foundation itself says that capture of stablecoin-issuer reserve income is zero and that "almost none" of RWA holder yield is captured. Bottom line: AVAX is a working gas-and-staking asset whose holders receive no meaningful cash flow today; the bull case is institutional adoption plus a future capture mechanism, neither of which yet shows up in burn.

### What the token is

- Ticker / name: AVAX (Avalanche). CoinGecko id avalanche-2, market-cap rank #26 (2026-11-10).

- Native asset, no contract on its home chain. AVAX exists natively on the P-Chain (staking, L1 management), X-Chain (UTXO transfers) and C-Chain (EVM, chain ID 43114). Smallest unit: 1 nAVAX = 10^-9 AVAX on P/X. On the C-Chain AVAX has 18 decimals (wei).

- Wrapped / bridged forms (verified on-chain 2026-11-10):

- WAVAX on C-Chain: 0xB31f66AA3C1e785363F0875A1B74E27b85FD66c7. symbol() = WAVAX; totalSupply = 17,538,729 WAVAX (re-read 16:20 UTC; 17,534,574 at 15:30 UTC).

- sAVAX (BENQI liquid staking) on C-Chain: 0x2b2C81e08f1Af8835a78Bb2A90AE924ACE0eA4bE. symbol() = sAVAX; totalSupply = 18,587,529 sAVAX (16:20 UTC). DefiLlama TVL is $201.1M, roughly 24M AVAX at the current price.

- Binance-Peg AVAX on BNB Chain: 0x1CE0c2827e2eF14D5C4f29a091d735A204794041. symbol() = AVAX; totalSupply = 2,000,000.

#### Supply (2026-11-10)

