#### Issuance / emission schedule

- Half of the cap (360M) was allocated at genesis (2020). The rest is minted only as staking rewards until the 720M cap is reached, so emission asymptotically tapers. Reward formula: Reward = (SupplyCap − CurrentSupply) × Staked/CurrentSupply × MintingRate × Duration/365d. MintingRate is linear between MinConsumptionRate and MaxConsumptionRate (12%), depending on stake duration ([docs](https://build.avax.network/docs/primary-network/avax-token)).

- Helicon (activated 2026-09-22) includes ACP-285, which lowers MinConsumptionRate from 10% to 7.5%. The cut phases in linearly over 90 days, ending around 2026-12-21, and applies only to stakes started after activation. A 48-hour stake goes from 10.011% to 7.525% "minting rate". A 1-year stake stays at 12%. After the remaining-supply multiplier ((720M − 476.0M)/476.0M ≈ 0.513 today), a 1-year stake earns about 6.15% simple (≈6.4% compounding with auto-renewal per the ACP-285 table) and the post-phase-in floor is about 3.85% (own calculation from the reward formula). The Foundation projects that inflation falls by 0.5–1.0 percentage point ([ACP-285](https://github.com/avalanche-foundation/ACPs/blob/main/ACPs/285-reduce-minimum-consumption-rate/README.md)).

- Realised issuance (estimate): ACP-285 quotes a supply of 470,134,316 AVAX for its reward calculations. Fact-check: that figure is already present in the first PR commit dated 2026-04-14 (GitHub API, PR #285), not first written at the 2026-06-11 merge. Today's counter is 475,987,384 (15:23 UTC). That is +5.85M AVAX in ≥210 days, i.e. at most ~10.2M AVAX per year. A second, independent estimate from the reward formula (195.8M staked × 5.1–6.15% ARR) gives ~10–12M AVAX/yr. Working figure: ~10–12M AVAX/yr (~2.1–2.5% of total supply; ~$82–99M/yr at $8.22). The Foundation states the trailing one-year inflation rate as ~5.5%, measured against "circulating" supply defined as issued minus burned minus staked (ACP-285), a much smaller base.

- Unlocks: the original vesting schedules (team, strategic partners, private sale) ended years ago. The remaining ~25M AVAX difference between CoinGecko total and circulating supply is mostly attributed by public trackers to the Foundation's long-dated quarterly vesting. This sheet could not verify a precise schedule from a primary source (Tokenomist, CryptoRank and DefiLlama unlock pages and APIs refused access, HTTP 403/402). Treat it as "not available". In scale, staking emission (~0.85–1.0M AVAX per month, estimate) is the dominant ongoing supply source.

- Largest holders / treasuries (partial):

- Avalanche Treasury Co. (Nasdaq: AVAT, debuted Thursday 2026-06-11 via the $675M Mountain Lake SPAC merger) was reported to hold "about 15 million" AVAX ([Cointelegraph](https://cointelegraph.com/news/avalanche-treasury-starts-trading-on-nasdaq-but-shares-fall-16-on-debut)).

- Bitwise's spot ETF BAVA (NYSE, launched 2026-04-15) stakes ~70% of its holdings.

- Exchange custody is large: DefiLlama attributes $344.7M of Avalanche-chain assets to Binance.

- Foundation and Ava Labs treasury balances are not published.

### How it works

#### Network architecture

- Primary Network = three chains validated by the same validator set:

- P-Chain: staking, validator registry, L1 creation and L1-validator fee accounting.

- X-Chain: UTXO asset transfers.

- C-Chain: EVM smart contracts, where almost all DeFi and RWA activity lives.

Consensus is Snowman/Avalanche (repeated random-subsample voting). Blocks currently come about once per second: 2.71M blocks between 2026-10-11 and 2026-11-10.

- Avalanche L1s (formerly "subnets"): app-specific chains with their own validator sets and VMs. Since Etna / ACP-77 (December 2024), L1 validators no longer need to stake 2,000 AVAX on the Primary Network. Instead they pay a continuous fee to the P-Chain, burned: 512 nAVAX/s, about 1.33 AVAX per month per validator while the network is below 10,000 active L1 validators ([ACP-77](https://github.com/avalanche-foundation/ACPs/blob/main/ACPs/77-reinventing-subnets/README.md)). The Avalanche Data API lists 583 subnets, 344 of them converted to L1s. 576 L1 validators across 69 L1s currently have a positive fee balance (re-count 2026-11-10 16:20 UTC; 581 / 70 at 15:30 UTC). Examples cited by the ecosystem: Progmat (Japan securities), the planned NYSE-affiliated clearing ledger, and gaming chains (whether each runs on its own L1 is not confirmed in the sources used here).

- Interoperability: Avalanche Warp Messaging / ICM (native cross-L1 messaging signed by validators, BLS).

#### Fees and burn

- A C-Chain transaction pays (base fee + priority tip) × gas. Both parts are burned by being credited to 0x0100…0000, which appears as miner in every block header. Validators get no fees. They are paid only by newly minted staking rewards ([Foundation, 2026-11-05](https://www.avax.network/about/blog/the-price-of-a-transaction-benchmarking-the-avalanche-c-chain-on-cost-and-capture)). The tip now makes up ~90% of what users pay, mostly from MEV searchers.

- History of the fee floor:

- 25 nAVAX until Etna (ACP-125, Dec 2024).

- 1 nAVAX until Fortuna (ACP-176, Apr 2025: EIP-1559-like continuous fee with a validator-voted gas target).

- 1 wei afterwards. The median base fee fell to 0.072 nAVAX in the 30 days before Helicon. Daily transactions rose ~11x (0.20M before Etna → 2.23M) while the price per unit of gas fell ~348x, and the C-Chain became one of the cheapest EVM chains: $7.91 per 1B gas in Aug-2026 vs $1,396 on Ethereum.

- Helicon / ACP-283 (2026-09-22) lets validators vote the minimum gas price continuously. The value is the stake-weighted median and can double or halve in about an hour.

- Observed on-chain since ACP-283 (this sheet's own reads of baseFeePerGas):

- ~0.06–0.18 nAVAX on 2026-09-23/26 (spot reads: 0.058 nAVAX 09-23 12:00 UTC, 0.165 nAVAX 09-26; 11.8 nAVAX at 09-29 12:00 during the move up).

- 5.0 nAVAX from ~2026-10-01.

- 2.5 nAVAX from ~2026-10-21.

- Ramped from 2.5 to 7.5 nAVAX between ~2026-11-09 23:20 UTC (header field minPriceExponent starts changing; it was constant through 2026-11-09 midday) and 2026-11-10 05:14:21 UTC (block 99,910,289, first block at exactly 7.5 nAVAX). Separately, on 2026-11-09 ~12:20–15:00 UTC (NYSE news) congestion pushed the base fee above the 2.5 floor (43.0 nAVAX at block 99,850,000, 12:37 UTC); that demand spike, not the floor change, produced the 3,992 AVAX burn of 2026-11-09.

Blocks are mostly near-empty (median gasUsed/gasLimit 0.7% over the last 1,024 blocks), so the floor is binding. Validators have raised the price of blockspace by roughly 40–125x against the pre-Helicon median.

- P-Chain and X-Chain fees are dynamic and multidimensional (ACP-103) and are also burned.

#### Staking

- A validator needs a 2,000 AVAX self-stake. The minimum duration is 48 hours (ACP-273; it was 2 weeks before Helicon), the maximum 1 year. Delegators need a 25 AVAX minimum. Delegation multiplier is 5x (total weight up to 5x self-stake, i.e. up to 4x self-stake delegated). ACP-247 (authors Giacomo Barbieri and BENQI) proposes raising the multiplier to 24x; status "Implementable", not yet activated.

- No slashing. A validator below the uptime threshold forfeits the period's reward, not principal. The threshold is 90% for stakes started after Helicon (ACP-267; it was 80%).

- Helicon added auto-renewing staking (ACP-236): a cycle renews automatically with a chosen reinvest share. Missing uptime ends the position.

- Liquid staking: BENQI sAVAX (~$201M TVL, DefiLlama 2026-11-10) is the main venue.

#### Governance

- There is no on-chain token vote. Protocol changes go through Avalanche Community Proposals (ACPs) on GitHub. They are activated by validators adopting new AvalancheGo releases, so stake-weighted node operators have the de facto vote. Several parameters are now continuously voted by validator node configuration: gas target (ACP-176), minimum block delay (ACP-226) and minimum gas price (ACP-283).

- Ava Labs writes most core code; Stephen Buttolph, Chief Protocol Architect, authored most recent core ACPs. The Avalanche Foundation funds grants and economic research.

#### Recent upgrades

- Etna (Dec 2024; ACP-77/103/125).

- Fortuna (Apr 2025; ACP-176).

- Granite (scheduled in AvalancheGo v1.14.0 released 2025-11-05: ACP-181 epoched P-Chain views, ACP-204 secp256r1/passkeys precompile, ACP-226 dynamic block times).

- Helicon (AvalancheGo v1.15.0 released 2026-09-08; activated on mainnet 2026-09-22 15:00 UTC): ACP-194 continuous/asynchronous execution, which separates acceptance from execution, plus ACP-283, 236, 273, 285 and 267. v1.15.2 (2026-10-22) removed the legacy Coreth code path. v1.15.3 shipped 2026-11-05 ([releases](https://github.com/ava-labs/avalanchego/releases)).

### Utility

- Real, protocol-enforced uses:

- Gas on the C-, P- and X-Chain. Every transaction must burn AVAX.

- Staking to validate the Primary Network: 2,000 AVAX per validator, plus delegation.

- Paying the continuous P-Chain fee for each L1 validator, about 1.33 AVAX per month (burned).

- Base collateral and unit of account in Avalanche DeFi (WAVAX, sAVAX in Aave V3/V4, BENQI, Pharaoh DEX pools).

- Not needed for:

- Gas on most Avalanche L1s. L1s can use their own gas token, so institutional L1s such as Progmat or a clearing ledger need AVAX only for the tiny P-Chain validator fee.

- Holding or transferring RWAs and stablecoins beyond tiny gas amounts.

- Governance votes (there is no token vote).

- Receiving any share of app revenue, stablecoin reserve yield or RWA fees. The Foundation states capture of stablecoin-issuer reserve income is "zero" and that "almost none" of holder yield is captured today ([GCI post, 2026-08-12](https://www.avax.network/about/blog/from-gross-chain-product-to-gross-chain-income-where-the-value-goes)).

- Net: AVAX is a working gas-and-security token with a small, real burn sink. It is not a cash-flow token. Holders who stake earn inflation (~3.85–6.4% ARR), which mostly redistributes value from non-stakers to stakers.

### Why people buy and sell it

#### Demand drivers

- Institutional / RWA narrative, the main current thesis:

- NYSE ledger selection (2026-11-09; AVAX +10% intraday, the top gainer in the top 100).

- BlackRock BUIDL plus Franklin Templeton, Apollo, KKR and Janus Henderson products.

- Goldman Sachs using Avalanche for payments/settlement through Lynq; Progmat (Japan) building institutional tokenization infrastructure on Avalanche (both per the [NYSE post](https://www.avax.network/about/blog/wall-streets-next-chapter-is-being-built-on-avalanche)). A reported migration of ¥452B of digital securities to an Avalanche L1 in July 2026 could not be verified from a primary source in this fact-check.

- UAE TDRA's UAEPASS (12.5M users) and DIFC Courts.

- Ethena Pay (exclusive to Avalanche).

- Aave Labs' planned RWA credit market with USA₮.

- Regulated access products:

- Bitwise BAVA spot ETF with staking (2026-04-15, 0.34% fee).

- Nasdaq 19b-4 filing for a VanEck Avalanche Trust (reported April 2026; no source link and final status not verified).

- CME AVAX futures (announced 2026-04-07 for launch on 2026-05-04 pending regulatory review; 5,000 AVAX and 500 AVAX micro contracts).

- Charles Schwab adding AVAX spot trading (announced 2026-08-27).

- Avalanche Treasury Co. (AVAT) on Nasdaq.

- Staking yield of ~3.85–6.4% nominal (Bitwise cited ~5.4% in mid-April 2026), now liquid within 48 hours for validators.

- Tokenomics reform narrative: the Foundation's three-step value-accrual agenda (measure, capture, distribute), the ACP-283 fee lever, ACP-285 lower inflation, and the ACP-67 stablecoin framework.

- Gas demand from DeFi and L1 validator fees, which is small in dollar terms.

#### Sell pressure

- Emissions: ~10–12M AVAX per year minted to stakers (estimate), about 22–27x the current annualized burn (~0.45M AVAX). Stakers who sell rewards create steady supply.

- Foundation and treasury vesting (~25M AVAX non-circulating per CoinGecko; schedule not verified).

- Macro and sector:

- Crypto bear market: BTC ~$74k on 2026-11-10; ETH −42% and SOL −50% over one year.

- The Binance infrastructure hack of 2026-10-29 (~$6.3B, multi-chain including Avalanche; DefiLlama).

- Weak digital-asset-treasury equities: AVAT −16% on debut.

- Rotation to competing chains for stablecoin, RWA and tokenized-stock activity (see "The protocol/business").

### The protocol/business

- What it does: a general-purpose EVM L1 (C-Chain) plus an "L1 factory" that lets companies, governments and apps launch their own chains (sovereign L1s) that interoperate natively. Commercial strategy, led by Ava Labs and AvaCloud (managed L1 infrastructure; CEO Nick Mussallem), now centres on institutions: capital markets, tokenized funds, private credit, payments, government records, ticketing and fan engagement ([NYSE post](https://www.avax.network/about/blog/wall-streets-next-chapter-is-being-built-on-avalanche)).

- Audience / where it is popular:

- US asset managers and fintechs (BUIDL, Janus Henderson JAAA, Avant savUSD, Tare private credit).

- Japan (Progmat) and Korea (historically).

- Middle East (UAE TDRA, DIFC Courts; Animoca Brands investment in Ava Labs 2026-03-19 targeting Asia and the Middle East).

- LatAm (Bolivia's telecom VIVA via Iris).

Retail DeFi activity on the C-Chain is modest: DEX volume $2.59B per 30 days, led by Pharaoh V3/DLMM ($1.89B combined), Uniswap V3 ($266M) and Blackhole ($129M).

- Top C-Chain apps by TVL (DefiLlama, 2026-11-10):

- Aave V3 $273.1M, Grove Finance $264.0M, BENQI sAVAX $201.1M, OpenTrade (RWA) $146.1M.

- Aave V4 $123.7M, Avant avUSD $106.9M, BENQI Lending $99.8M.

Top fee earners over 30 days: BlackRock BUIDL $1.58M, Centrifuge $1.15M, Grove $1.04M, BENQI sAVAX $0.95M, Pharaoh V3 $0.91M. The chain's own gas came to $0.33M.

- Trend:

- TVL $1,485M (2025-11-10) → $607M (2026-11-10), −59%. Peak $11.49B in Dec 2021.

- Stablecoins $2.35B → $1.26B, −46%. Peak $4.70B in Mar 2022.

- Validators 854 (2025-10-28, per ACP-247) → 541 (2026-11-10 16:16 UTC), −37%.

- RWA on Avalanche passed $1.3B at end-2025 (Messari via [Cointelegraph](https://cointelegraph.com/news/blackrock-buidl-helps-avalanche-tokenization-value-q4)), and >$1.65B by June 2026 per the ecosystem figure quoted in the [Cointelegraph AVAT article](https://cointelegraph.com/news/avalanche-treasury-starts-trading-on-nasdaq-but-shares-fall-16-on-debut).

