### Revenue and value capture

On Avalanche the three layers collapse into one: (a) gross fees = (b) protocol revenue = (c) value to holders, because 100% of C-Chain fees are burned and nothing else accrues to the protocol. There is no treasury fee switch and no buyback. Mechanism: the fee of every C-Chain transaction is credited to the burn address 0x0100000000000000000000000000000000000000 (block miner), from which no one can spend. The burn reduces supply pro rata for all holders. Separately, P-Chain and X-Chain fees and the L1-validator continuous fee are destroyed at UTXO level on the P/X chains.

| Period | DefiLlama "Avalanche" fees = revenue = holders revenue (USD) | On-chain C-Chain burn (AVAX), this sheet's reads | Window of on-chain read |

| --- | --- | --- | --- |

| Last full UTC day (2026-11-09) | $34,849 | 3,991.9 AVAX (~$34.8k at $8.73) | blocks 99,802,702 → 99,892,498 |

| Rolling 24h | $36,561 at 15:20 UTC, then $22,411 at 16:10 UTC (DefiLlama "total24h" = provisional day 2026-11-10; it is revised during the day) | 2,126.3 AVAX (~$17.6k) | 2026-11-09 15:38 → 2026-11-10 15:38 UTC |

| 7 days | $87,194 | 10,906.4 AVAX (~$90.5k) | 2026-11-03 15:38 → 2026-11-10 15:38 UTC |

| 30 days | $331,216 | 37,958.3 AVAX (DefiLlama-implied 36,956) | 2026-10-11 00:00 → 2026-11-10 15:23 UTC |

| 12 months | $2,674,572 | 264,524.3 AVAX (DefiLlama-implied 261,079) | 2025-11-10 00:00 → 2026-11-10 |

| Annualized (last 30d run-rate) | ~$4.0M | ~452,000 AVAX/yr (~$3.7M at $8.22) | estimate |

| All-time (burn address balance) | $92.46M (DefiLlama all-time fees and revenue; all-time holders revenue is $90.89M — the series differ only in early history) | 5,139,736.6 AVAX | to 2026-11-10 15:38 UTC |

- Cross-check: converting DefiLlama's daily USD with CoinGecko daily prices gives AVAX amounts within 0.5–3% of the on-chain burn-address deltas for every window: 2026-08-12→09-22: 26,281 vs 26,108; 09-22→10-11: 32,565 vs 32,732; last 30d: 36,956 vs 37,958; 1y: 261,079 vs 264,524. For DefiLlama's latest, in-progress day (2026-11-10), the value moved from $36,561 to $22,411 within an hour while on-chain shows only ~1,337 AVAX (15:38 UTC) / ~1,436 AVAX (16:16 UTC) burned so far that day (~$11–12k), so that point is provisional. Use the last full day instead. Note also that DefiLlama total7d/total30d cover full UTC days only (2026-11-03..09 and 2026-10-11..11-09), slightly different from the on-chain windows.

- Trend:

- Annual fees: $63.5M (2023, inscriptions mania), $17.9M (2024), $8.35M (2025), $1.99M (2026 through 2026-11-09).

- Monthly fees bottomed at $59.6k (Jul-2026).

- After Helicon and the validator-voted floor increase they rose to $335.7k (Sep-2026) and $368.5k (Oct-2026).

- Daily burn went from ~640 AVAX before Helicon (Aug 12–Sep 22) to ~1,720 AVAX (Sep 22–Oct 11) and ~1,240 AVAX (last 30d). So ACP-283 roughly doubled to tripled daily burn, while transactions per block fell sharply: ~17 tx/block in late Aug–Sep vs ~2.6 tx/block in the last 30 days (random sample of 150 blocks each; estimate). An independent re-sample of 120 blocks each gave 18.8 vs 3.9 mean tx/block (medians 12.5 vs 2), i.e. ~80% fewer. The floor priced out spam such as XEN proof-of-work minting, which was ACP-283's stated aim.

- P-Chain L1 validator fees (estimate): 576–581 L1 validators with a positive balance × 512 nAVAX/s (16.1 AVAX/yr each) ≈ 9,300–9,400 AVAX per year (~$77k), all burned. This is not tracked by DefiLlama.

- Net value to holders: burn (~0.45M AVAX/yr run-rate) is ≈4–5% of issuance (~10–12M AVAX/yr). AVAX is net inflationary by roughly 9.5–11.5M AVAX/yr (~2.0–2.4% of total supply; estimate). Fees are ~3.39% of app revenue on Avalanche (Jan-2025–Aug-2026), falling to 1.13% in Aug-2026 (Foundation benchmarking post). Avalanche apps earned ~$282.2M of protocol revenue and ~$87.1M retained ("holder/treasury" share) over that period, against ~$9.6M of chain transaction fees.

- Income the ecosystem generates but AVAX does not capture (Foundation GCI estimates, June 2026):

- On-chain value added (NGCP) $3.1M per month.

- Holder yield (BUIDL, JAAA, Avant etc.) $2.7M per month; $32.3M lifetime.

- Stablecoin-issuer reserve income $6.9M per month; $242.8M lifetime, ~96% from the two largest issuers ($173.2M and $59.7M). The Foundation says capture of this layer is "zero"; for holder yield "almost none" is captured.

Burned gas was ~3% of monthly NGCP.

- Stated plan to monetize:

- Use ACP-283's floor as a lever on fee capture, with demand-elasticity experiments promised.

- "Voluntary revenue sharing" by protocols and L1s in exchange for public goods, distribution and liquidity (research and BD stage).

- A protocol-owned or aligned stablecoin with yield sharing ([ACP-67 discussion](https://github.com/avalanche-foundation/ACPs/discussions/293)).

- Lower untargeted inflation (ACP-285).

"Step three: distribution" to the token is not yet designed ([GCI post](https://www.avax.network/about/blog/from-gross-chain-product-to-gross-chain-income-where-the-value-goes); Summit 2026 keynote by Foundation economist Matias A., 2026-09-17).

### How to verify on-chain

No API key is needed for the calls below. Etherscan V2's free tier does not serve chain 43114 (checked 2026-11-10: "Free API access is not supported for this chain"), so use Routescan's free Etherscan-compatible endpoint for block-by-time lookups. Values obtained on 2026-11-10 are shown after each command.

#### 1. Cumulative C-Chain burn (burn address balance)

curl -s https://api.avax.network/ext/bc/C/rpc -H 'content-type: application/json' \ -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"eth_getBalance","params":["0x0100000000000000000000000000000000000000","latest"]}'# result hex wei / 1e18 → 5,139,736.56 AVAX at block 99,948,534 (15:38 UTC)# fact-check re-run → 0x440670c8a1adb99e64fae = 5,139,835.65 AVAX at 16:16 UTC (block ~99,951,002)

For a period, query the same address at a historical block. api.avax.network served archive state in this run; publicnode did not:

# block at a timestamp (UTC seconds)curl -s "https://api.routescan.io/v2/network/mainnet/evm/43114/etherscan/api?module=block&action=getblocknobytime&timestamp=1791676800&closest=before"# → 97238723 (2026-10-11 00:00 UTC)curl -s https://api.avax.network/ext/bc/C/rpc -H 'content-type: application/json' \ -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"eth_getBalance","params":["0x0100000000000000000000000000000000000000","0x5cbbec3"]}'# → 5,101,730.56 AVAX ; delta to now = 37,958 AVAX burned in ~30.6 days

Reference points read for this sheet:

| Date (UTC) | Block | Burn address balance (AVAX) |

| --- | --- | --- |

| 2025-01-01 00:00 | 55,159,596 | 4,552,969.74 |

| 2025-11-10 00:00 | 71,706,577 | 4,875,164.61 |

| 2026-08-12 00:00 | 92,595,357 | 5,042,890.11 |

| 2026-09-22 00:00 (Helicon day) | 95,870,563 | 5,068,998.24 |

| 2026-10-11 00:00 | 97,238,723 | 5,101,730.56 |

| 2026-11-09 00:00 | 99,802,702 | 5,134,407.70 |

| 2026-11-10 00:00 | 99,892,498 | 5,138,399.58 |

| 2026-11-10 15:38 | 99,948,534 | 5,139,736.56 |

#### 2. Confirm that fees go to the burn address and read the current fee floor

curl -s https://api.avax.network/ext/bc/C/rpc -H 'content-type: application/json' \ -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"eth_getBlockByNumber","params":["latest",false]}'# "miner":"0x0100000000000000000000000000000000000000", "baseFeePerGas":"0x1bf08eb00" (=7.5 nAVAX; re-confirmed block 99,951,002, 16:16 UTC),# "gasLimit":"0x4c4b400" (80M), header also carries "minPriceExponent" (ACP-283 vote state)curl -s https://api.avax.network/ext/bc/C/rpc -H 'content-type: application/json' \ -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"eth_feeHistory","params":["0x400","latest",[50]]}'# last 1,024 blocks: base fee min/median 7.5 nAVAX, max 8.30; median gasUsedRatio 0.0073# re-run 16:16 UTC (blocks 99,950,206+): min/median 7.5, max 8.37; median gasUsedRatio 0.0076

#### 3. Supply counter and staking

curl -s https://api.avax.network/ext/bc/P -H 'content-type: application/json' \ -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"platform.getCurrentSupply","params":{}}'# → {"supply":"475987384020241602","height":"25840706"}  (nAVAX; 475,987,384 AVAX; excludes burns)# re-run 16:16 UTC → {"supply":"475987469562853412","height":"25840989"}curl -s https://data-api.avax.network/v1/networks/mainnet# → validatorCount 542; validators totalAmountStaked 154,577,399 AVAX; delegatorCount 38,186;#   delegators totalAmountStaked 42,194,218 AVAX; stakingRatio 0.4134# re-run 16:16 UTC → validatorCount 541; 153,554,399 AVAX; delegatorCount 38,260; 42,199,031 AVAX; stakingRatio 0.4113

#### 4. L1 validator fee payers

curl -s "https://data-api.avax.network/v1/networks/mainnet/l1Validators?pageSize=100"   # paginate with pageToken# 2,014 L1 validator records; 581 with remainingBalance > 0 across 70 L1s (fee: 512 nAVAX/s each, burned)# re-count 16:20 UTC → 2,009 records; 576 with remainingBalance > 0 across 69 L1s

#### 5. Aggregators (second source)

curl -s "https://api.llama.fi/summary/fees/avalanche?dataType=dailyHoldersRevenue"   # total7d 87194, total30d 331216, total1y 2674572 (re-confirmed 16:10 UTC)curl -s "https://api.llama.fi/v2/historicalChainTvl/Avalanche"                        # 605.7M on 2026-11-10curl -s "https://stablecoins.llama.fi/stablecoincharts/Avalanche"                     # 1.252B on 2026-11-10curl -s "https://api.coingecko.com/api/v3/coins/avalanche-2?localization=false&tickers=false"

#### 6. Token contracts

# symbol() = 0x95d89b41, totalSupply() = 0x18160dddcurl -s https://api.avax.network/ext/bc/C/rpc -H 'content-type: application/json' \ -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"eth_call","params":[{"to":"0xB31f66AA3C1e785363F0875A1B74E27b85FD66c7","data":"0x18160ddd"},"latest"]}'# WAVAX totalSupply 17,534,574.48 (15:30 UTC); 17,538,729.09 (16:20 UTC)# Binance-Peg AVAX on BSC: same call to https://bsc-rpc.publicnode.com with "to":"0x1CE0c2827e2eF14D5C4f29a091d735A204794041" → 2,000,000

Pitfalls:

- getCurrentSupply is not "total supply". It adds pending rewards and ignores burns.

- The burn-address balance counts only C-Chain burns, not P/X-Chain fees.

- Anyone can send AVAX to 0x0100… voluntarily, which would inflate it slightly.

- Glacier "metrics" endpoints (metrics.avax.network) returned implausible gaps for Apr and Aug–Nov 2026 in this run, so they were not used.

