### Current problems and risks

- Value capture is tiny and the token is net inflationary. ~$0.33M per month of burn against ~$82–99M per year of issuance at current prices (estimate). The Foundation itself states capture of issuer reserve income is zero, of holder yield "almost none", and that chain fees equal ~1–3% of app revenue. Every reform (revenue sharing, protocol stablecoin) is still at the research stage.

- Institutional wins route little to AVAX. Deals like NYSE, Progmat and UAEPASS typically run on dedicated L1s where AVAX is needed only for ~1.33 AVAX per month per validator fee. The NYSE ledger's token and fee design has not been disclosed. The ecosystem narrative and token economics are decoupled: Messari data showed RWA TVL up nearly 950% in 2025, while Cointelegraph noted AVAX fell nearly 60% in Q4 2025.

- Shrinking on-chain economy:

- TVL −59% y/y to $607M, ranked #12, behind Robinhood Chain, Monad and Polygon.

- Stablecoins −46% y/y to $1.26B (stablecoincharts; $1.22B and #12 on stablecoinchains), behind Circle's Arc ($1.30B).

- Chain fees −68% (2025 vs 2024).

- C-Chain transaction count fell sharply after the fee-floor increase (estimate: ~80–85% fewer tx per block, two independent samples).

- Validator-set contraction / centralization: 854 validators (Oct-2025) down to 541 (2026-11-10). 52.8% of validators had zero delegations in Oct-2025 (ACP-247). Validator economics are thin at low AVAX prices.

- Fee-policy uncertainty: the validator-voted floor moved 0.07 → 5.0 → 2.5 → 7.5 nAVAX within seven weeks. That is good for burn, but it makes costs less predictable for apps. The Foundation says the demand elasticity is unknown.

- Competition for the "institutional chain" role from Ethereum and its L2s (Base), Solana (first SEC-framework tokenized stock venue, CoinDesk 2026-11-09), purpose-built chains (Circle Arc, Robinhood Chain, Stripe-backed and Tether-backed chains), Canton and DTCC's own tokenization service (Oct-2026), and ICE/OKX's tokenized-stock platform (CoinDesk 2026-11-09). Nasdaq/Kraken reportedly plan tokenized stocks for Q2-2027 (DTCC and Nasdaq/Kraken items not re-verified in the fact-check).

- Security incidents in the ecosystem: Fence Finance exploit ($1.01M, 2026-10-27), and multi-chain CEX hacks touching Avalanche (Binance, Mercado Bitcoin). No Avalanche-protocol-level incident was found.

- Leadership turnover: President change in Aug-2026. The co-founders other than Sirer are no longer on the team page.

- Treasury and ETF vehicles under pressure: AVAT fell on debut, and digital-asset-treasury equities are down sharply sector-wide. Any forced selling by such vehicles would add supply.

- Macro: broad crypto bear market (BTC ~$73.4k on 2026-11-10 16:14 UTC; AVAX −24% over 30d; a Fed rate increase is being priced per CoinDesk 2026-11-10).

What the bulls believe: Avalanche is becoming the default infrastructure for regulated finance (NYSE, BlackRock, Franklin, Apollo, KKR, Progmat, UAE government, Schwab distribution, ETFs). The Foundation now openly targets value accrual, and validators have shown they will use ACP-283 to raise burn. Lower inflation (ACP-285) and longer staking reduce float. So a re-rating could come if any of the capture mechanisms ship while institutional volume grows.

### What would move the token

| Catalyst | Timing | Bullish if | Bearish if |

| --- | --- | --- | --- |

| ACP-283 floor votes (C-Chain min gas price) | continuous; currently 7.5 nAVAX | Burn stays ≥1,500 AVAX per day on a sustained basis without losing real users | Floor cut back, or activity migrates and burn falls back to ~600 AVAX per day |

| ACP-285 phase-in complete | ~2026-12-21 (Helicon + 90 days) | Issuance drops 0.5–1 pp and stake duration lengthens | Staking ratio falls (currently 41.1%) |

| NYSE-affiliated tokenized platform go-live and its design | "upcoming"; could launch before end-2026 if approved by regulators (WSJ via Cointelegraph) | Platform or its L1 uses AVAX for fees or collateral, or shares revenue | Permissioned L1 with its own gas token: headline only |

| Foundation value-capture design (revenue sharing, ACP-67 stablecoin) | no dates; "step two" research | Concrete ACP with fee routing to burn or stakers | Continued research with no mechanism |

| Schwab AVAX trading launch; VanEck ETF; CME AVAX futures volumes | "coming months" (Schwab, announced 2026-08-27) | New US retail and institutional access, ETF inflows | Outflows from BAVA, weak futures OI |

| ACP-247 (24x delegation multiplier) | Implementable; not scheduled | Better validator economics, stable validator count | Further validator attrition |

| Stablecoin and RWA float on Avalanche (USA₮/Aave RWA hub, Ethena Pay, BUIDL) | ongoing | Stablecoins back above $2B, RWA growth | Continued decline (−46% y/y) |

| Competitor tokenized-stock venues (Solana, Nasdaq/Kraken Q2-2027, DTCC) | 2026–2027 | Avalanche remains the settlement layer of record | Flagship institutions pick other chains |

| Macro / CEX security fallout (Binance hack) | ongoing | Risk-on recovery | Further deleveraging |

