As of 2026-11-10. Live numbers were pulled between 14:40 and 16:30 UTC on 2026-11-10 unless another date is given. The reference NEAR block is 223,934,461 (2026-11-10 15:23:58 UTC). Prices are in USD. "Fees", "revenue" and "holders revenue" follow DefiLlama's definitions unless stated otherwise. Bracketed numbers such as [1] refer to the Sources section. The web-search budget for this run ran out early. News and people therefore come from primary sources fetched directly: the NEAR blog, the governance forum, the on-chain House of Stake contract, GitHub, Bitwise and DefiLlama. Items not confirmed this way are marked "not verified".

### Executive summary

NEAR is the native token of NEAR Protocol, a sharded proof-of-stake Layer-1 launched in 2020. NEAR pays for gas and storage, secures the chain through staking, and since 2025 gives voting power in House of Stake governance (as veNEAR). The network's main business is no longer the L1 itself but NEAR Intents, a cross-chain swap and settlement product. Intents settled $3.73B of volume and charged $5.62M of gross fees in the last 30 days [8][10]. L1 gas is tiny by comparison: $157k over 30 days [7]. Value does reach holders today, but it is small next to dilution. Intents revenue is used to buy NEAR on the open market. In the last 30 days the two main revenue wallets accumulated about 395k NEAR (about $1.5–1.8M), and DefiLlama counts $1.84M of holders revenue. Over the same period about 2.69M NEAR of new issuance was created at the 2.5% cap. Net supply still grows by about 2.48% a year, measured on-chain (1,279.58M → 1,311.34M NEAR, 2025-11-10 → 2026-11-10) [3][4]. The bought-back NEAR sits in a multisig and a DAO wallet. It is not burned. The token is in a post-hype correction. It rose about 6x from a 1-year low of $0.96 (2026-02-12) to $5.89 (2026-10-12), helped by record Intents volume and the launch of a US spot ETF (Bitwise NRR, 2026-09-28). It traded at $3.56 on 2026-11-10 16:12 UTC, down 38.4% over 30 days and about 40% below the October peak [1][2][32]. The single most important thing to watch is the ratio of Intents buybacks to emissions, together with two inputs to it. One is whether HSP-029 (cut issuance from 2.5% to 1.6% over 24 months; passed, in timelock until about 2026-11-16) is actually activated by validators. The other is whether bought-back NEAR is formally burned or locked [15][16]. Status in one line: real and growing product revenue, but holder value today is a discretionary, custodial buyback that offsets only about 15% of gross issuance.

### What the token is

- Ticker / native asset: NEAR. Native token of NEAR Protocol mainnet (genesis 2020-07-21) [5]. Denomination: 1 NEAR = 10^24 yoctoNEAR.

- Representations on other chains / wrappers (verified on-chain 2026-11-10):

- wNEAR (NEP-141) on NEAR: wrap.near, ft_total_supply 36,725,564 wNEAR (2026-11-10 16:15 UTC) [3].

- Ethereum: NEAR (Rainbow Bridge ERC-20) 0x85F17Cf997934a597031b2E18a9aB6ebD4B9f6a4, name "NEAR", 24 decimals, totalSupply 4,356,644 [43].

- BNB Chain: "NEAR Protocol" BEP-20 (Binance-peg) 0x1Fa4a73a3F0133f0025378af00236f3aBDEE5D63, 18 decimals, totalSupply 12,950,000 [43].

- Market (CoinGecko, re-fetched 2026-11-10 16:12 UTC) [1]: price $3.56; market cap $4.664B (rank #21); 24h volume $474.2M; 30d −38.4%; 1y +25.4%; all-time high $20.44 (2022-01-16). 1-year range: low $0.964 (2026-02-12), high $5.89 (2026-10-12) [2].

