#### Issuance / emission schedule

- Current cap: max_inflation_rate = 1/40 = 2.5% per year of total supply, minted per epoch (43,200 blocks) [5]. The cap was 1/20 (5%) at protocol version 77 (block 160,000,000, 2025-08-17) and 1/40 at version 81 by block 172,000,000 (2025-11-10) [4]. The "halving" activated on mainnet at block 170,351,519 (2025-10-29 11:29 UTC, protocol version 80 → 81, max_inflation_rate [1,20] → [1,40]; located by binary search on archival EXPERIMENTAL_protocol_config) [4][45]. On-chain supply growth fell from ≈172k NEAR/day (2025-09-21 → 10-12) to ≈87k NEAR/day after 2025-11-06 [4].

- Split: about 90% goes to validators and delegators and about 10% to treasury.near (the protocol treasury). Note that the protocol_reward_rate config field reads 0/1 and is not a reliable indicator [15]. I measured it myself: treasury.near grew +202,410 NEAR (1,352,309 → 1,554,719) between blocks 219,650,000 and 222,934,461 (2026-10-12 → 2026-11-03). Total supply grew +1,997,806 NEAR in the same window, so the treasury share is about 10.0% of gross issuance [4].

- Gross issuance today: about 2.5% × 1,311M / 365 ≈ 89.8k NEAR/day, or about 32.8M NEAR a year (≈$117M/yr at $3.56). The HSP-029 author cites 89,500 NEAR/day [17] and a measured realized gross issuance of 2.45%/yr with a 10.13% treasury share [15].

- Approved cut (pending implementation): HSP-029 lowers the cap linearly from 2.5% to 1.6% over 24 months, about 3.75 bp per month, per epoch. It keeps the 90/10 split. It avoids an estimated 11.8M NEAR of issuance over 2 years and 66.1M over 6 years (author's model). On-chain status of proposal #29 on vote.dao: "Timelock". Voting started 2026-10-19 16:48 UTC and lasted 14 days. The result was 3,287,729 veNEAR For (32 voters), about 0 Against and 1,071 veNEAR Abstain, against 5,274,745 veNEAR at snapshot, with a 66.67% approval threshold. A 14-day timelock follows, ending about 2026-11-16 [16]. It also needs a nearcore protocol upgrade adopted by validators. The text says "activation occurs one full quarter after ratification", with a 90-day grace period, so the first reduction is unlikely before about mid-Feb 2027 [15].

#### Unlocks

No vesting cliffs remain. NEAR's own tokenomics post (2026-02-24) states "the network's token supply is now fully unlocked" [11]. The only scheduled new supply is protocol issuance, about 89.8k NEAR/day. Secondary supply sources are the treasury (treasury.near, 1,614,436 NEAR on 2026-11-10 [3]) and the HoS-administered programs that spend emissions-funded treasury assets, such as the HSP-007 MPC node program [23].

