NEAR Foundation's own token holdings were not verified in this run. The Foundation says it has "500M funds raised" [42], but no current treasury report was retrieved.

### How it works

#### The chain

- Consensus and sharding: proof-of-stake with "Nightshade" sharding. The live shard layout is V3 with 10 shards, at protocol version 88 and nearcore 2.14.0 [5]. Blocks are produced about every 0.58–0.6 s: ≈146.4k blocks/day measured over 2026-10-12 → 11-10 (4,284,461 blocks in 29.26 days), and the epoch that started at block 223,876,337 lasted 6 h 54 min (2026-11-10 06:07 → 13:01 UTC) [4]. Epoch = 43,200 blocks (≈7 h). The configured num_blocks_per_year of 31,536,000 is a legacy 1-block-per-second parameter; issuance is computed per epoch and the measured supply growth (≈2.46%/yr) matches the 2.5% cap minus burn [4][5]. 100 block-producer seats; the full validator set is 338 [6]. Recent upgrades include stateless validation, dynamic resharding (announced 2026-05-20), a Wasmtime runtime (2.12.0), a 1 PGas contract gas limit (2.11.0), ML-DSA post-quantum signatures, and "SPICE" separation of consensus and execution, presented as part of Nightshade 3.0 at NEARCON 2026 [13][30][44][46][47].

- Accounts: human-readable named accounts (e.g. alice.near), multiple access keys per account, and native account abstraction. Since 2026-09-21, Top-Level Accounts (governed by House of Stake as registrar under HSP-028) and free "Recovery Keys" are live [29].

- Gas: fees are paid in NEAR. The current gas price is the floor of 100,000,000 yoctoNEAR per gas unit, i.e. 0.0001 NEAR per Tgas (gas_price RPC, 2026-11-10) [3]. A simple transfer costs about 0.00005 NEAR (≈$0.0002).

- Fee burn: before 2026-11-04, 70% of gas was burned and 30% was paid to the called contract's account (the "developer rebate"). HSP-027 removed the rebate: the vote passed with 4.67M veNEAR For (started 2026-06-28), and it shipped in nearcore 2.14.0 (released 2026-10-26), which upgrades the protocol from version 86 to 88 in two steps. The rebate removal took effect with protocol version 87 at block 223,012,337 (2026-11-04 11:46:29 UTC): block 223,012,336 reads PV86 with burnt_gas_reward [3,10], block 223,012,337 reads PV87 with [0,1]. Protocol version 88 followed at block 223,314,737 (2026-11-06 12:17:42 UTC) with no further change to this parameter. Both boundaries were located by binary search on archival EXPERIMENTAL_protocol_config (fact-check re-derivation) [4][13][14][16]. Since then, 100% of gas is burned.

- Storage staking: accounts must lock NEAR in proportion to the on-chain state they use (about 1 NEAR per 100 kB under the long-standing parameter). This locks NEAR but does not burn it.

- Staking: validators run staking-pool contracts; holders delegate. In the standard staking-pool contract, unstaked NEAR becomes withdrawable after 4 epochs (NUM_EPOCHS_TO_UNLOCK = 4), i.e. about 28 h at the current ≈7 h epoch length [50]. Rewards come only from issuance; fees are burned, not paid to validators. The 90-day average gross staking reward rate is quoted by Bitwise as 5.00% (2026-11-08) [32]. Bitwise quotes a net (after its staking fee) rate of 3.35% as of 2026-11-07 [32]. The HSP-029 author measured a gross yield of 5.268% at a 42.71% staking ratio on 2026-09-22 [15]. Liquid-staking tokens (e.g. Rhea LST) exist.

#### Governance — House of Stake (HoS)

- HoS went live on mainnet in October 2025 [45]. Holders lock NEAR in a per-user lockup contract via venear.dao and receive non-transferable veNEAR. veNEAR grows at a fixed rate over time; unlocking takes 45 days (unlock_duration_ns 3,888,000 s) [16]. Proposals are voted on in vote.dao. The owner is hos-root.sputnik-dao.near. Gauntlet (gauntletgov.near) reviewed proposals 24–25 (HSP-007, constitutional documents); proposals 27–29 (HSP-027, HSP-028, HSP-029) list arrr_tems.near as reviewer [16].

- Participation is low: veNEAR total supply is 5,392,219 (2026-11-10 16:15 UTC), about 0.41% of NEAR supply [16]. Economic-policy votes (rebate removal, issuance cut) passed with 3–5M veNEAR. HoS ratification still needs validator adoption for protocol parameters [15].

- HoS reports 11 proposals processed in "Season #1" [19].

#### NEAR Intents — the main product

- A user (or agent, wallet or app) states an outcome, e.g. "swap 1 BTC on Bitcoin into USDC on Solana". A network of competing solvers (market makers) quotes and fills it. Settlement happens atomically in the intents.near Verifier contract, which keeps an internal multi-token ledger [26][10].

- Assets enter and leave through bridges and Chain Signatures. Examples are the omft.near token factory for bridged assets [38] and Chain Signatures, an MPC network run by 17 independent operators that signs transactions on other chains, with all signing inside TEEs since October 2026 [23][24]. Coverage is "35+ chains", EVM and non-EVM [25][27].

- Products built on it: near.com (NEAR's own front-end, launched 2026-02-24; confidential trading by default), 1Click API for integrators, Confidential Intents (general availability 2026-07-07; confidential TVL $139.6M on 2026-11-09, +371.6% over 90 days) [10], NEAR Business (confidential multisig treasury, 2026-10-20) [25], tokenized US stocks via Ondo on near.com (2026-09-22) [28], and the Talos OEMS integration for institutions (2026-11-09) [26].

- Fees (official dashboard FAQ): a protocol fee of 0.0001% per swap plus distribution fees set by integrators. Swaps through near.com send 100% of fees to a NEAR revenue wallet; swaps through third-party integrators split fees 50/50. All revenue-share payouts are denominated in NEAR [10][11]. The measured effective gross fee rate is 15.1 bp on the last 30 days (fees ÷ volume from the dashboard series) [10].

#### NEAR AI

- NEAR AI (founded by Illia Polosukhin) runs NEAR AI Cloud: TEE-hosted private inference on Intel TDX plus NVIDIA confidential computing, with an OpenAI-compatible API. Named users include Brave (Leo) and Venice. It also runs Private Chat, an Agent Market (54 pay-per-job agents live per a 2026-11-02 forum post) and IronClaw agents [41][12][49].

- Since 2026-07-30, users can pay for NEAR AI by staking NEAR: the stake is converted into monthly compute credits, and all 43 models are available this way [31]. NEAR's tokenomics post says compute and agent services are "payable in $NEAR" [11]. No public NEAR AI revenue figure was found.

### Utility

- Real, protocol-enforced utility:

- gas for every NEAR transaction, now 100% burned;

- storage staking for on-chain state;

- proof-of-stake security, through validator and delegator staking;

- veNEAR voting power in House of Stake;

- a payment rail for NEAR AI via staking credits.

- Economic link to Intents: Intents users do not need to hold NEAR. Swaps are between BTC, USDC, ZEC and other assets, and solvers pay NEAR gas. The token link is indirect: NEAR-controlled wallets convert Intents fee revenue into NEAR and hold it, and partner rev-share payouts are made in NEAR [10][11].

- What it is NOT needed for: using near.com, 1Click or third-party front-ends (users pay in the asset they swap); bridging assets; holding tokenized stocks.

- Holder rights: NEAR carries no legal claim on Intents revenue. The tokenomics post states that "token holders have no entitlement to the execution of any particular mechanism", and that governance keeps discretion over buybacks, locking or redistribution [11].

### Why people buy and sell it

#### Demand drivers

- Revenue-backed buybacks: since the fee switch (late Feb 2026), Intents revenue buys NEAR. Monthly revenue per the official dashboard: Aug $0.87M, Sep $2.20M, Oct $2.50M [10].

- "Chain abstraction / market of markets" narrative: NEAR Intents is one of the largest cross-chain swap venues. Its $3.73B 30-day volume is above THORChain's $2.75B and Chainflip's $0.89B [36]. It is a common route for Zcash (ZEC) swaps [21].

- AI narrative: co-founder Illia Polosukhin co-authored "Attention Is All You Need". The pitch is "AI money": confidential inference, agent payments and x402 Foundation membership (2026-07-14) [12][51].

- Regulated wrappers: the Bitwise NEAR ETF (NRR) launched on NYSE Arca on 2026-09-28; AUM was $56.96M (15.69M NEAR) on 2026-11-08, fee 0.75%, 100% staked [32]. Listed ETPs named by NEAR in July 2026: Bitwise and 21Shares staking ETPs, Virtune, Grayscale NEAR Trust (GSNR) and Valour. A Grayscale NEAR ETF filing was described as pending; its current status was not verified [12].

- Treasury company bid: SVRN holds about 55M NEAR (≈4.2% of supply), mostly staked [15].

- Supply-policy narrative: the halving (2025), rebate removal (2026-11-04), the HSP-029 cut toward 1.6%, and a forum discussion on a "path to a fixed supply" [17].

- Staking yield: about 5% gross, the reason to hold rather than just trade.

#### Supply / sell pressure

- Issuance: about 89.8k NEAR/day (≈$320k/day at $3.56). This is roughly 5x the 30-day average Intents buyback flow of ≈$61k/day (DefiLlama 30d holders revenue ÷ 30).

- Staker selling: the HSP-029 author measured about 54.5M NEAR unstaked in the two weeks to 2026-09-22 while price rose 86%. The staking ratio fell from 46.92% to 42.71% [15]. It was 44.3% on 2026-11-10 [6].

- Treasury and program spending from treasury.near (≈10% of issuance), e.g. MPC node payments and the HoS operating budget [16][23].

- Speculative flows: NEAR fell about 40% from the 2026-10-12 peak ($5.89) to $3.56 (2026-11-10 16:12 UTC). NRR's NAV fell 20.15% over the month to 2026-10-30 [1][2][32].

### The protocol/business

- What it does: a general-purpose L1 that has repositioned itself as "a unified commerce layer for assets and agents". It has three product pillars:

- NEAR Intents: cross-chain execution;

- Chain Signatures: MPC signing for other chains;

- NEAR AI: confidential AI and agents [11].

- Audience:

- wallets and exchanges integrating 1Click (Ledger Live, Infinex, KyberSwap, SimpleSwap, SwapKit and others are named on the NEAR blog);

- retail traders using near.com, especially privacy-minded ones (confidential swaps, ZEC);

- institutional desks (Talos OEMS);

- crypto teams (NEAR Business treasury);

- AI developers (NEAR AI Cloud) [11][21][25][26].

- Where it is popular: activity on the NEAR L1 itself has shrunk sharply. NearBlocks 30-day averages to 2026-11-08 compared with a year earlier [34]:

- 661k transactions/day, down from 4.47M;

- 57.5k daily active accounts, down from 264k (daily figures rose to 77–79k on 2026-11-03 → 11-09);

- 9.4k new accounts/day, down from 223k.

Peaks were 13.9M transactions (2023-12-01) and 2.26M active accounts (2024-04-22). The largest legacy apps by state are game.hot.tg (HOT wallet), Sweat, KaiKai and Aurora, which appear as shard boundary accounts [5]. The growth is in Intents, which serves users on other chains.

