### Revenue and value capture

#### (a) Gross fees paid by users

| Stream | 24h (2026-11-09) | 7d | 30d | 1y | Source |

| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |

| NEAR L1 gas | $3,341 | $21,780 | $157,206 | $1.170M | DefiLlama "near" [7] |

| NEAR Intents gross fees (protocol + distribution) | $57,866* | $1.342M | $5.619M | $53.70M | DefiLlama "near-intents" [8]; dashboard 30d sum $5.617M [10] |

| Near Perps (Hyperliquid builder fees) | $1,742 | $13,687 | $109,410 | $214k | [9] |

*The 2026-11-09 Intents fee figure looks incomplete. Volume that day was $166M, yet fees were only $57.9k (3.5 bp) against $190–255k on the previous days (14–16 bp). Use the 7d and 30d figures.

#### (b) Protocol revenue

- L1: the gas burn. DefiLlama still models 70% of fees as burned ($110k over 30d). Since 2026-11-04 11:46 UTC (PV87) the burn is 100% of fees. My on-chain cross-check: sampling 192 random blocks from the last ~24h (sum of chunk balance_burnt) gives about 0.0058 NEAR burned per block; at the measured ≈146–150k blocks/day that is ≈850–870 NEAR/day (≈$3.1k/day). An independent 22-block re-sample by the fact-checker (blocks 223.8M–223.93M) gave 0.00584 NEAR/block. NearBlocks reports 923 NEAR of transaction fees on 2026-11-09 [34]. Annualized, the burn is ≈0.30–0.34M NEAR, about 1% of gross issuance.

- Intents: NEAR's captured ("net") revenue was $58.4k (24h), $372.8k (7d), $1.838M (30d) and $9.30M (1y) per DefiLlama [8]. The official dashboard shows Oct 2026 at $2.502M (512,857 NEAR) and cumulative revenue since Aug 2025 of $11.56M (5.02M NEAR) [10]. The dashboard headline "$18.58M" is a different measure: cumulative protocol burn plus gross revenue.

#### (c) What actually reaches token holders

| Channel | 7d | 30d | Annualized | Mechanism |

| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |

| Gas burn (L1) | ≈5.8k NEAR | ≈25k NEAR (≈$0.1M) | ≈0.3M NEAR (≈$1.1M) | Burned in protocol; 100% since 2026-11-04 (PV87) |

| Intents buyback (DefiLlama holders revenue) | $372.8k | $1.838M | ≈$22.4M (30d × 12.17) | Revenue converted to NEAR and held; DefiLlama counts all captured revenue since 2026-02-23 as buyback [8] |

| Intents buyback (my on-chain wallet deltas) | +95.6k NEAR (2026-11-03 → 11-10) | +395.2k NEAR (2026-10-12 → 11-10) | ≈4.9M NEAR | buybacks.multisignature.near +279,227 / +68,986; fefundsadmin.sputnik-dao.near +115,988 / +26,647 [3][4] |

| For comparison: gross issuance | ≈629k NEAR | ≈2.69M NEAR (≈$9.6M at $3.56) | ≈32.8M NEAR (≈$117M at $3.56) | 2.5% cap, 90% stakers / 10% treasury |

- Conclusion: the buybacks plus burn offset roughly 15% of gross issuance on 30-day data. Holders' net position is still about +2.4–2.5% supply inflation a year. Measured as a yield on market cap, the buyback is about 0.48% a year ($22.4M ÷ $4.66B market cap on 2026-11-10). Stakers are compensated by the ~5% gross staking yield. Non-stakers (≈56% of supply) are diluted.

- Exact mechanism (observed on-chain):

- Fees are collected inside the intents.near ledger in whatever asset was swapped.

- Revenue is swept to the NEAR-controlled wallets: fefundsadmin.sputnik-dao.near (near.com front-end fee fund, a Sputnik DAO), 1csfundsadmin.sputnik-dao.near (1Click and partner rev-share fund) and buybacks.multisignature.near (a multisig created 2026-03-18).

- Assets are swapped to NEAR via Intents and withdrawn as native NEAR. NearBlocks shows dozens of small inbound receipts per day from intents.near into buybacks.multisignature.near, e.g. 25 inflows between 2026-11-09 14:31 and 2026-11-10 15:27 UTC [33].

Dashboard all-time flow attribution: fefundsadmin 1,994,014 NEAR (46.6%), buybacks multisig 1,730,368 (40.4%), 1csfundsadmin 555,348 (13.0%) [10]. The NEAR is held, not burned. The only outgoing multisig requests found were a 12,000 NEAR transfer to an implicit account (request 2026-07-09) and test transfers of 20 and 5 NEAR to nf-payments.near (March 2026). The last 200 balance activities show no outbound flows [33]. Illia Polosukhin wrote on 2026-08-20 that buyback NEAR should "never come back to circulation", but that "the proposed mechanism doesn't guarantee" it [18].

- Stated plan: per the tokenomics post, "a governance-based treasury structure is being established" to receive all product revenue (Intents, AI, future products). Tools it may use: ad-hoc buybacks, "buyback and earn" (staking or locking the bought NEAR), and other supply management. "No specific mechanism is guaranteed" [11]. A draft "Sovereign Yield Engine" HSP (2026-11-08) proposes putting part of Intents fees into T-bills and venture investments [40]. It is a draft only.

### How to verify on-chain

All commands are public and need no API key. NEAR amounts are in yoctoNEAR (divide by 1e24). Use https://rpc.mainnet.near.org or https://rpc.fastnear.com for current state, and https://archival-rpc.mainnet.fastnear.com for historical blocks. These endpoints rate-limit; space requests about 1 s apart.

#### 1. Total supply, gas price (my reading: 1,311,344,236.5 NEAR at block 223,934,461; gas price 100,000,000)

curl -s https://rpc.mainnet.near.org -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \ -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"block","params":{"finality":"final"}}' \ | jq '.result.header | {height, timestamp_nanosec, total_supply, gas_price}'# historical: replace params with {"block_id":172000000} on the archival endpoint -> 1,279,576,328 NEAR (2025-11-10)

#### 2. Inflation cap, fee burn share, shard count (mine: max_inflation_rate [1,40]; burnt_gas_reward [0,1]; protocol_version 88; 10 shards)

curl -s https://rpc.fastnear.com -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \ -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"EXPERIMENTAL_protocol_config","params":{"finality":"final"}}' \ | jq '.result | {protocol_version, max_inflation_rate, epoch_length, num_blocks_per_year,   burnt_gas_reward: .runtime_config.transaction_costs.burnt_gas_reward,   shards: (.shard_layout.V3.shard_ids|length)}'# with {"block_id":223012336} on archival -> PV86, burnt_gas_reward [3,10]; {"block_id":223012337} -> PV87, [0,1] (rebate removed 2026-11-04 11:46 UTC)# {"block_id":170351518} -> PV80, max_inflation_rate [1,20]; {"block_id":170351519} -> PV81, [1,40] (halving, 2025-10-29)

#### 3. Staked supply (mine: 581.29M NEAR across 338 validators)

curl -s https://rpc.fastnear.com -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \ -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"validators","params":[null]}' \ | jq '[.result.current_validators[].stake|tonumber]|add/1e24'

#### 4. Buyback and revenue wallets (mine on 2026-11-10: 2,233,872 / 1,997,195 / 271 NEAR; treasury.near 1,614,436)

for a in buybacks.multisignature.near fefundsadmin.sputnik-dao.near 1csfundsadmin.sputnik-dao.near treasury.near; do curl -s https://rpc.fastnear.com -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \  -d "{\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":1,\"method\":\"query\",\"params\":{\"request_type\":\"view_account\",\"finality\":\"final\",\"account_id\":\"$a\"}}" \  | jq -r --arg a $a '"\($a) \(.result.amount|tonumber/1e24)"'; done# 30d delta: repeat with "block_id":219650000 (2026-10-12) on the archival endpoint -> buybacks 1,954,645; fefunds 1,881,207# inflow detail (sender = intents.near):curl -s 'https://api.nearblocks.io/v1/account/buybacks.multisignature.near/activities?per_page=25' \ | jq '.activities[] | {block_timestamp, direction, involved_account_id, absolute_nonstaked_amount}'

#### 5. Daily gas burn (mine: ≈0.0058 NEAR/block, ≈850–870 NEAR/day)

# tokens burnt in one block = sum of chunk balance_burnt for chunks included at that heightcurl -s https://rpc.fastnear.com -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \ -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"block","params":{"block_id":223900000}}' \ | jq '[.result.chunks[] | select(.height_included==223900000) | .balance_burnt|tonumber] | add/1e24'# multiply the average over many blocks by ~146,000-150,000 blocks/day (measure: height difference of two blocks a day apart); cross-check: NearBlocks daily txn_feecurl -s https://api.nearblocks.io/v1/charts | jq '.charts | sort_by(.date) | .[-3:] | .[] | {date, txn_fee, txns, active_accounts}'

#### 6. Intents fees / revenue / buybacks (DefiLlama and official dashboard)

curl -s 'https://api.llama.fi/summary/fees/near-intents?dataType=dailyFees' | jq '{total24h,total7d,total30d,total1y}'curl -s 'https://api.llama.fi/summary/fees/near-intents?dataType=dailyHoldersRevenue' | jq '{total24h,total7d,total30d,total1y}'curl -s 'https://api.llama.fi/summary/fees/near?dataType=dailyFees' | jq '{total24h,total7d,total30d}'# official: https://revenue.near.org (wallet table + monthly revenueSeries embedded in page data)

#### 7. Governance state (mine: proposal 29 status "Timelock", For 3,287,729 veNEAR)

ARGS=$(echo -n '{"proposal_id":29}' | base64 -w0)curl -s https://rpc.fastnear.com -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \ -d "{\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":1,\"method\":\"query\",\"params\":{\"request_type\":\"call_function\",\"finality\":\"final\",\"account_id\":\"vote.dao\",\"method_name\":\"get_proposal\",\"args_base64\":\"$ARGS\"}}" \ | jq -r '.result.result|implode' | jq '{status, voting_start_time_ns, votes, timelock_duration_ns}'# veNEAR supply: same call with account_id "venear.dao", method "ft_total_supply", args {} -> 5,392,219 veNEAR

#### 8. Bridged token supply (Ethereum)

curl -s https://ethereum-rpc.publicnode.com -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \ -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"eth_call","params":[{"to":"0x85F17Cf997934a597031b2E18a9aB6ebD4B9f6a4","data":"0x18160ddd"},"latest"]}'# hex result / 1e24 = 4,356,644 NEAR on Ethereum

