### 3. How it works

#### The chain

- Consensus: PlasmaBFT, a pipelined Fast-HotStuff derivative. It needs n ≥ 3f+1 validators, uses stake-weighted committee selection, and penalizes misbehavior by reward slashing, not stake slashing. Validators are not penalized for liveness failures ([consensus docs](https://docs.plasma.org/docs/plasma-chain/architecture/consensus.md)). The site claims ~1 s blocks and ~3 s deterministic finality ([plasma.org/network](https://www.plasma.org/network)). I measured 100,000 blocks in 100,072 s, i.e. 1.0007 s per block, from block 37,281,344 to 37,381,344 on 2026-11-09/10.

- Execution: Reth-based EVM. Ethereum contracts deploy unchanged.

- Validator rollout: three stages: (1) trusted validators at launch, (2) validator expansion, (3) permissionless participation. The consensus-node page still describes "future consensus node operation". Staked delegation is "planned". I found no evidence that external validators or delegation are live as of 2026-11-10 ([docs](https://docs.plasma.org/docs/node-operators/consensus-preparation/preparation.md)).

- Zero-fee USD₮ transfers: plain USD₮0 transfers are sponsored through authorization-based transfers and a protocol-run relayer/paymaster. At launch this was limited to Plasma's own products (app.plasma.to, Plasma One), with a stated plan to open it more widely ([mainnet blog](https://www.plasma.org/company/blog/plasma-mainnet-beta-and-xpl)). Everything else pays gas in XPL.

- Custom gas tokens: planned. A protocol-maintained paymaster would let whitelisted ERC-20s (e.g. stablecoins) pay gas "without charging a fee". Today only XPL is accepted as gas ([network fees docs](https://docs.plasma.org/docs/plasma-chain/network-information/network-fees.md)).

- Assets: USD₮0 (LayerZero OFT version of Tether) 0xB8CE59FC3717ada4C02eaDF9682A9e934F625ebb, supply 972.74M (on-chain, 2026-11-10 16:16 UTC). Also Ethena USDe/sUSDe, weETH and native USDC via Circle Bridge Kit. The default bridge is Stargate.

#### Token mechanics

- Gas: all non-sponsored transactions pay gas in XPL, using standard EIP-1559 fields.

- Burn (documented): "base fees paid to transact on the Plasma blockchain are permanently burned" (tokenomics docs). In practice: the base fee was 8 wei (0.000000008 gwei) in every one of the last 1,024 blocks at 15:40 UTC and 8–13 wei at the 16:16 UTC re-check (eth_feeHistory, 2026-11-10). In sampled blocks the burn was roughly 4–8×10⁻¹¹ XPL per block, which is economically zero.

- Priority fees: in three blocks with fees that I checked one by one (37,381,759 / 763 / 764), 100% of tips were credited to the block coinbase 0x…0a11b005; the coinbase balance change equaled the tips exactly. That address is a Gnosis Safe proxy (v1.4.1, masterCopy 0x29fcb43b46531bca003ddc8fcb67ffe91900c762) with an 8-owner, 5-signature threshold. Its 7 executed transactions are six owner swaps plus one MultiSend (2025-11-12, a value-0 CALL to MultiSendCallOnly 0x9641d764fc13c8b624c04430c7356c1c7c8102e2), and it has never sent XPL out.

- Staking / inflation: validator rewards are designed to start at 5% annual inflation, falling by 0.5 percentage points per year to 3%. They activate only when external validators and delegation go live. Locked team and investor XPL cannot earn rewards. Changes need a validator vote once delegation is live.

- Governance: there is no token governance, DAO or on-chain voting. Plasma (the Cayman company) runs the protocol and treasury.

- Locked XPL Vault (Plasma One): users can unlock Plasma One Core by paying $199/year or locking 20,000 XPL for 12 months. Platinum can be unlocked only by locking XPL: 100,000 XPL for 12 months (≈$5.3k at $0.0527) per the [Platinum page](https://www.plasma.org/personal/platinum) (2026-11-10); the Rewards Addendum says amounts are set in the Help Center and may change. Locks pay no yield and grant no governance rights. The vault is "administered by a Plasma-controlled timelocked multisig" ([Core page](https://www.plasma.org/personal/core), [Rewards Addendum](https://www.plasma.org/plasma-one-rewards)). The vault contract address is not published on those pages and was not located in this run.

- XPL as reward currency: Plasma One cashback (2–4% base, up to 10% in categories) and referral rewards accrue in USD and are paid in XPL or Spending Credit, at Plasma's choice. A built-in "Cash Out" swaps XPL to USD through the 0x aggregator ([Rewards Addendum](https://www.plasma.org/plasma-one-rewards)).

#### How users experience it

Consumers use Plasma One (iOS and Android). It offers a stablecoin balance, a Visa card, local-currency on-ramps, zero-fee USD₮ sends between users, and "Earn" (DeFi vaults, P1USD). Most users never touch XPL except as cashback. DeFi users bridge USD₮0, USDe or weETH into Aave, Fluid, Euler, Pendle and similar protocols on Plasma, and pay small XPL gas for those interactions. Builders deploy EVM contracts and integrate USD₮ payment flows.

### 4. Utility

| Use | Real today? | Notes |

| --- | --- | --- |

| Gas for non-sponsored transactions | Yes, but tiny | Total gas spend was $6,340 in 30 days (DefiLlama). Plain USD₮ transfers are sponsored, so the main use case needs no XPL. |

| Plasma One Core/Platinum tier access via 12-month lock | Yes (Core: 20,000 XPL lock or $199/yr; Platinum: 100,000 XPL lock only) | This is the only demand sink that removes XPL from circulation. Locked amount: not available. |

| DeFi collateral / liquidity / incentives | Yes | WXPL pools (Uniswap V3, Fluid, etc.). Incentives paid in XPL add to sell pressure. |

| Staking for security / yield | No (planned) | Delegation and inflation rewards are not live per docs. |

| Claim on fees (fee share, buyback, burn) | No | The base-fee burn is ≈0. Tips go to a team-controlled multisig. |

| Governance | No | There is no token voting. |

| Gas for USD₮ transfers | No (by design) | The planned paymaster lets apps hide XPL entirely. |

### 5. Why people buy and sell it

#### Demand drivers

- "Stablecoin chain" narrative: backed by the Tether/Bitfinex orbit (Bitfinex/USD₮0 co-led the $24M round, Paolo Ardoino was an angel), Founders Fund and Peter Thiel, and Framework. It competes in the 2026 stablecoin-L1 category with Tether's Stable, Circle's Arc and Stripe's Tempo.

- Plasma One growth: TVL went from $1.07M (2026-05-07) to $30.87M (2026-11-10) ([DefiLlama](https://api.llama.fi/protocol/plasma-one)). XPL locks are required for the top tier.

- Price near the public-sale price: the public sale and the Founders Fund equity round were both priced at a $500M FDV, i.e. $0.05 per XPL ([sale blog](https://www.plasma.org/company/blog/announcing-the-xpl-public-sale-using-sonar-by-echo)). Spot price is $0.0527 (FDV $527M, 2026-11-10 16:15 UTC). Some buyers treat this level as an anchor.

- Listings: the largest venues by 24h volume are LBank, Binance (USDT and USDC pairs), Upbit (KRW), WhiteBIT, CoinW, Bybit, OKX, Bithumb (KRW), Gate, Bitget, Kraken (USD) and MEXC ([CoinGecko tickers](https://api.coingecko.com/api/v3/coins/plasma/tickers)). CoinGecko category tags include "Binance HODLer Airdrops". Korean KRW markets are material: Upbit had $2.5M of 24h volume.

- Speculation on future value accrual: staking and inflation launch, a real burn, or a fee switch.

#### Supply / sell pressure

- Unlocks: ≈227.8M XPL per month until September 2028 (ecosystem + team + investors). The team and investor cliff on 2026-09-25 released ≈1.667B XPL. CoinGecko market cap jumped from $249M (2026-09-07) to $506M (2026-09-27), which was mostly supply. Price fell from $0.1116 (2026-09-27) to $0.0527 (2026-11-10).

- US public-sale unlock on 2026-07-28. The portion of the 1B sale bought by US accredited buyers is not disclosed.

- Incentive dumping: XPL paid as DeFi incentives (Aave, Binance Earn 100M) and as Plasma One cashback and referral rewards, with one-tap cash-out to USD built in.

- No structural sink: no burn of any size and no buyback.

### 6. The protocol/business

Company: "Plasma, an exempted company with limited liability incorporated under the laws of the Cayman Islands". Affiliates are Plasma Labs UK Ltd., Plasma MENA FZE and Plasma US, Inc. HQ is in London ([Terms of Service, effective 2026-11-06](https://www.plasma.org/terms-of-service); [About](https://www.plasma.org/company/about)). The company now brands itself as a fintech ("financial technology company, not a regulated financial institution") building a "global dollar account". The domain moved from plasma.to to plasma.org.

#### Product lines

- Plasma chain: a stablecoin-payments L1 (see section 3).

- Plasma One (announced with a waitlist on 2025-09-22; live in 2026, DefiLlama-tracked TVL from 2026-05-07; Android launch promo ended 2026-07-21): stablecoin neobank and Visa card.

- Tiers: Lite (free, 2% cashback), Core ($199/yr or 20,000 XPL lock; 3% base cashback, degressive by monthly spend (3% on the first $1,000, then 2%/1%/0.25%), and 5% AI-spend cashback up to $500/month; ChatGPT Go), Platinum (100,000 XPL lock only; 4% base, degressive (4%/3%/2%/1%), and 10% on AI and flights; Claude Pro + ChatGPT Plus; lounge access) ([Core](https://www.plasma.org/personal/core) and [Platinum](https://www.plasma.org/personal/platinum) pages, 2026-11-10).

- Card issuers per ToS of 2026-11-06: Third National with Rain as program manager, Lead Bank (Member FDIC) on Stripe Issuing, Stripe Payments UK (UK), Stripe Technology Europe (EEA). Account rails: Bridge (a Stripe company). UAE: AED accounts with Ruya.

- Plasma Business: corporate cards, global payouts, treasury yield.

- Licensing: acquired a VASP-licensed entity in Italy; Netherlands compliance hub; planned MiCA CASP and EMI applications ([blog 2025-10-22](https://www.plasma.org/company/blog/licensing-our-payments-stack-to-reach-global-scale)). Current license status after that post was not verified.

#### Audience and geography

The stated focus is dollar-hungry markets: Istanbul, Buenos Aires, Dubai and LatAm/MENA ([Plasma One blog](https://www.plasma.org/company/blog/introducing-plasma-one-the-one-app-for-your-money), [Founders Fund blog](https://www.plasma.org/company/blog/accelerating-global-stablecoin-adoption-with-founders-fund)). Marketing now also targets "AI spend" consumers in the US, UK and EU. On the DeFi side the audience is yield farmers and loopers on Aave/Fluid (USD₮0, USDe/sUSDe, weETH). The network page claims "50+ countries, 25+ currencies, 50M+ merchants, $250B+ annual transfer volume" (marketing, not verified).

