### 7. Revenue and value capture

#### (a) Gross fees paid by users (chain gas)

| Period | DefiLlama "plasma" dailyFees (USD) | On-chain: coinbase Safe balance growth (XPL) | On-chain ≈USD |

| --- | --- | --- | --- |

| Last 24h | $44 (2026-11-09) | +730.5 XPL (blocks 37,294,944 → 37,381,344); re-check +876.4 XPL (blocks 37,297,590 → 37,383,990) | ≈$39–46 at $0.0527–0.0536 |

| Last 7d | $637 | +9,689 XPL (re-check +9,834) | ≈$520 at spot (price was falling, so the USD figure at historical prices is somewhat higher) |

| Last 30d | $6,340 | +83,804 XPL (re-check +83,890) | ≈$4.4k at spot; DefiLlama uses daily prices (~$0.06–0.08 in October), hence $6.3k |

| Last 60d | n/a | +248,146 XPL (re-check +248,187) |  |

| Annualized (30d × 12.17) | ≈$77k | ≈1.02M XPL |  |

| Trailing 1y | $110,891 |  |  |

| All-time (since 2025-09) | $272,086 | 1,167,587.2 XPL accumulated balance (16:16 UTC) | ≈$61.5k at $0.0527 |

Monthly gas fees (DefiLlama) peaked in October 2025 at $87.9k. Since then: Dec 2025 $7.5k, Mar 2026 $4.3k, May 2026 $0.5k, Sep 2026 $19.2k, Oct 2026 $7.4k. The two sources agree: the on-chain XPL growth of the coinbase Safe matches DefiLlama's USD figures once you account for price changes.

#### (b) Protocol revenue

Effectively $0 at the token/protocol level. DefiLlama's methodology for Plasma reads "Revenue: Burned coins", and it books 100% of fees as both Revenue and Holders Revenue ($6,340 over 30d). On-chain data contradicts that label. The base fee is 8–13 wei, so the burn rounds to zero. All fees are priority tips, and they accumulate in the 5-of-8 multisig 0x…0a11b005, which I assume is controlled by Plasma or the trusted validators (the owners are not publicly labeled). Treat DefiLlama's "holders revenue" for Plasma as a misclassification.

Company-level revenue, which does not flow to XPL: Plasma One Core subscriptions ($199/yr), card interchange (via Rain/Stripe programs) and FX/ramp spreads. No figures are disclosed.

Ecosystem revenue that accrues to other tokens: Aave V3 on Plasma generated $2.96M of fees over 30d (DefiLlama Plasma fees breakdown). That money goes to Aave suppliers and the Aave DAO, not XPL.

#### (c) Value reaching XPL holders

| Channel | 24h | 30d | Mechanism |

| --- | --- | --- | --- |

| Burn (EIP-1559 base fee) | ≈0 XPL (<10⁻⁵ XPL est.) | ≈0 | baseFeePerGas = 8–13 wei |

| Buyback | 0 | 0 | None announced or observed |

| Staking distributions | 0 | 0 | Delegation not live |

| Fee share | 0 | 0 | None. Tips sit in the multisig; zero XPL has been sent out. |

Stated plan to monetize or accrue value:

- Launch external validators and delegation. Stakers would then earn 5%→3% inflation, which is dilution, not revenue ([tokenomics](https://docs.plasma.org/docs/get-started/xpl/tokenomics.md)).

- Rely on the EIP-1559 burn to "balance new emissions" as usage grows. With the base fee at 8–13 wei this needs either a base-fee policy change or a large rise in congestion.

- Use Plasma One as distribution, with XPL as the lock asset for tiers and as the cashback currency.

- The docs say the "Core Protocol roadmap" includes "dedicated payment lanes … and custom fee structures". No public fee-switch proposal was found.

### 8. How to verify on-chain

All commands below use public endpoints. Replace YOUR_KEY with your own Etherscan V2 key where needed. Values I obtained are shown after each command.

#### Chain basics and the base fee (burn check)

curl -s -X POST https://rpc.plasma.to -H 'content-type: application/json' \ -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"eth_feeHistory","params":["0x400","latest",[50]]}'

Result (2026-11-10): baseFeePerGas = 0x8 (8 wei) in all 1,024 blocks; average gasUsedRatio 0.10. Fact-check re-run (2026-11-10 16:16 UTC, latest block 37,383,996): base fee values 8–13 wei (0x8–0xd), average gasUsedRatio 0.128, miner still 0x…0a11b005. Latest block 37,381,196 had baseFee 8 wei, gasUsed 3,021,709, gasLimit 36,000,000, 12 tx, miner 0x…0a11b005.

#### Fee recipient: balance over time

# current balance (XPL, 18 decimals)curl -s -X POST https://rpc.plasma.to -H 'content-type: application/json' \ -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"eth_getBalance","params":["0x000000000000000000000000000000000a11b005","latest"]}'# same at a past block (archive supported): replace "latest" with a hex block number, e.g. 0x2391360 (37,294,944 ≈ 24h earlier)

Results: 1,167,425.58 XPL at block 37,381,344 (fact-check re-run: 1,167,587.24 XPL at block 37,383,990, 16:16 UTC; 1,166,710.79 at −86,400 blocks; 1,083,697.17 at −2,592,000 blocks). Earlier values: 1,166,695.05 (−86,400 blocks), 1,157,736.07 (−7d), 1,083,621.29 (−30d), 919,279.24 (−60d), 643,361.88 (block 22,381,344), 373,935.55 (block 7,381,344).

#### Prove that tips (not burns) are the fees

# for block N: sum(gasUsed*(effectiveGasPrice-baseFee)) over eth_getBlockReceipts(N)#  == eth_getBalance(coinbase,N) - eth_getBalance(coinbase,N-1)curl -s -X POST https://rpc.plasma.to -H 'content-type: application/json' \ -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"eth_getBlockReceipts","params":["0x23A6684"]}'

Result: blocks 37,381,764 / 763 / 759 had tips of 0.016170 / 0.017316 / 0.012040 XPL, equal to the coinbase balance changes; burns were 8.1×10⁻¹¹ / 3.7×10⁻¹¹ / 3.5×10⁻¹¹ XPL.

#### Who controls the fee recipient (Safe)

