Primary sources only; press coverage was not reviewed (see the research note at the top).

- 2026-11-06: new Terms of Service. Plasma One cards are now offered under two US programs: Third National/Rain, and Lead Bank on Stripe Issuing. UK cards are issued by Stripe Payments UK and EEA cards by Stripe Technology Europe. A UAE addendum adds AED accounts with Ruya. Named affiliates: Plasma Labs UK, Plasma MENA FZE, Plasma US Inc. ([ToS](https://www.plasma.org/terms-of-service))

- 2026-11-09: XPL set its all-time low of $0.050342, right at the $0.05 public-sale price. Spot price on 2026-11-10 was $0.0527 (16:15 UTC), down 41% over 30d ([CoinGecko](https://api.coingecko.com/api/v3/coins/plasma)).

- Oct–Nov 2026: chain TVL fell from $551.7M (2026-10-29) to $426.3M (2026-11-10). Over the same window stablecoin supply rose from $1.335B (10-19) to $1.506B (11-10), and Plasma One TVL rose from $13.16M (10-04) to $30.87M (11-10) (DefiLlama).

- 2026-10-23: Aave governance proposal "[Direct-To-AIP] Onboard PT-sUSDe-28JAN2027 to Aave V3 Plasma Instance" ([forum](https://governance.aave.com/t/direct-to-aip-onboard-pt-susde-28jan2027-to-aave-v3-plasma-instance/25902)).

- 2026-10-01: engineering post "Pass the torch". It describes Torch, a new validator-committee handoff mechanism for PlasmaBFT that is needed for validator-set changes, i.e. groundwork for external validators ([blog](https://www.plasma.org/company/blog/pass-the-torch)).

- 2026-09-28: "Card Service Disruption" incident; 2026-09-15: scheduled maintenance ([status page](https://statuspage.incident.io/plasmanetwork)).

- 2026-09-25: team and investor 1-year cliff (≈1.667B XPL) and the start of 24-month linear vesting. The Platinum Referral Boost closed to new referrals the same day and was replaced by Upgrade Bonuses for referrals from 2026-09-26 ([Boost terms](https://www.plasma.org/platinum-referral-rewards), [Rewards Addendum](https://www.plasma.org/plasma-one-rewards)).

- 2026-09-27: CoinGecko market cap rose from $249M (09-07) to $506M as circulating supply jumped; price peaked locally at $0.1116.

- Earlier context, outside 90 days: 2026-07-28 US public-sale unlock; 2026-07-23 Platinum Referral Boost start (XPL-paid); Plasma One Android launch (promo ended 2026-07-21).

### 11. Current problems and risks

- No value accrual: about $77k of annualized fees against a $251M market cap and $527M FDV (2026-11-10). The burn is economically zero, and fees go to a team-controlled multisig. DefiLlama's "holders revenue" overstates value capture.

- Unlock overhang: ≈228M XPL per month (≈4.8% of circulating, ≈$12.0M at $0.0527) through September 2028, plus 5.24B still locked. Every month brings team, investor and ecosystem supply into a falling market.

- Mercenary-liquidity decay: TVL went from $6.36B (Oct 2025) to $0.43B, a 93% drop. Stablecoins went from $6.35B to $1.51B. Aave deposits on Plasma peaked at $6.6B in mid-October 2025 (gross deposits, per Plasma's blog); today Aave V3 Plasma shows $357.0M net TVL plus $672.9M borrowed, i.e. ≈$1.03B gross supplied (DefiLlama, 2026-11-10). The growth was incentive-driven, and incentives were paid in XPL.

- The main use case needs no XPL: zero-fee USD₮ transfers and planned stablecoin gas abstraction mean the most-used product does not require XPL.

- Centralization: trusted validator set, no live delegation, fees custodied in a 5/8 multisig, no token governance, and a single Cayman company controlling the roadmap, treasury and Locked XPL Vault.

- Competition: Tether is backing Stable and Circle has Arc ($1.29B of USD stablecoins already, close to Plasma's $1.50B). Tempo (Stripe) has $0.82B. Plasma's card partner Stripe is also a competitor through Tempo. Tron still dominates USD₮ payments with $93.6B of USD stablecoins and $24.5M of 30-day fees.

- Business-model divergence: Plasma One revenue (subscriptions, interchange) accrues to the company's equity, not to XPL. XPL is used mainly as a cashback currency, which creates continuous sell flow, and as a lock asset.

- Regulatory: the company runs consumer card programs in the US, UK, EEA and UAE. MiCA CASP and EMI licensing was still in progress as of the last primary-source update. Card-program changes, such as the 2026-09-28 disruption and the ToS of 2026-11-06 that lists a second US card program (Lead Bank on Stripe Issuing) alongside Third National/Rain, are an operational risk.

- Hopes and narratives that still support the token: Plasma One traction, Tether-ecosystem alignment, price near the $0.05 sale/VC anchor, and an eventual staking launch.

