Unlock math. The original gross unlock was 267,187,500 ENA a month to April 2028, as Blockworks Advisory stated on 2026-08-27 [17]. That equals 93.75M + 78.125M + 40.625M + 54.6875M. With investor tranches accelerated, I estimate the remaining scheduled flow at about 189.06M ENA a month, or about $28M a month at $0.1495 (2026-11-10), until about March 2028. Foundation and ecosystem tokens are released at Foundation discretion, so actual market supply may be lower.

StablecoinX. StablecoinX is a Nasdaq-listed ENA treasury company (ticker "USDE", trading since June 2026 [19]). The Foundation calls it "one of the top two largest holders of ENA at approximately 20% of total supply", subject to lockups in its SEC-filed Token Purchase Agreement [11]. Per the filing, locked ENA bought in the 2025-07-21 PIPE structure cannot be transferred for 48 months after the agreement. 25% unlocks at the 12-month anniversary of closing and the remaining 75% in 36 monthly installments. A follow-on purchase of 914,341,825.83 locked ENA on 2025-09-05 has the same structure [28]. The exact closing dates, and therefore the first StablecoinX unlock date, were not verified.

