### 3. How it works

#### The product: USDe and sUSDe

- Minting and redeeming. Only approved, KYC/KYB'd market makers ("Mint Users") can mint or redeem USDe directly. US persons are not eligible [28]. They deposit USDT, USDC or USDtb (and historically BTC/ETH/LSTs) into the MintRedeem V2 contract 0xe3490297a08d6fC8Da46Edb7B6142E4F461b62D3 [8]. Minting with USDC became free in July 2026 and with USDT in August 2026 (0 bps) [18]. Others buy on DEXs (mainly Curve; DEX liquidity ≈$49M at Q3-end) or exchanges [18]. On 2026-11-10 the MintRedeem contract held $31.1M USDC, $30.2M USDT and $11.9M USDtb available for redemptions (on-chain read).

- Backing. Volatile assets (BTC, ETH, SOL, XRP, BNB, and since Aug–Sep 2026 tokenized equities and gold) are held spot and hedged with an equal short perpetual, so the dollar value stays roughly flat and the protocol collects funding paid by leveraged longs. Stable assets (stablecoins, overcollateralized loans, tokenized T-bill/CLO funds) are held unhedged [10]. Backing sits off-exchange with custodians (Copper, Ceffu for Binance, Anchorage, Kraken Custody) and in Coinbase on-chain wallets [13].

- sUSDe. USDe holders stake into the ERC-4626 vault 0x9D39A5DE30e57443BfF2A8307A4256c8797A3497. Each week a subsidiary of the Ethena Foundation mints USDe rewards into the StakingRewardsDistributor 0xf2fa332bd83149c66b09b45670bce64746c6b439, which drips them into the vault every ~8 hours [4]. On-chain on 2026-11-10: 1.2079B USDe staked (24.3% of supply); 1 sUSDe = 1.25755 USDe. Rewards are "discretionary"; negative periods are not passed to sUSDe but absorbed by the Reserve Fund [4][5]. The unstaking cooldown became dynamic (1, 3, 5 or 7 days) in March–April 2026 and has been 1 day since activation [21][18].

- Reserve Fund. Multisig 0x2b5ab59163a6e93b4486f6055d33ca4a115dd4d5 (4/10 signers) [8]. It holds $62.04M per the Ethena API (2026-11-10 12:59 UTC) [31]. On-chain this was verified as 42.02M USDtb plus 19.98M USDtb-USDC Curve LP (virtual price 1.0048 → ≈$20.08M), ≈$62.1M in total. The share of revenue sent to the fund is currently 0% [5]. It has received no allocation since 2024-12-12 [17].

- USDtb. USDtb is a separate fiat-style stablecoin backed mainly by tokenized T-bills (BUIDL). It has been issued by Anchorage Digital Bank since October 2025 [9]. On-chain Ethereum supply is 416.9M (DefiLlama all chains: $447M), down from about $889M in June 2026 [19].

#### The token: ENA and sENA

- Governance. ENA holders vote on Snapshot (ethenagovernance.eth), mainly to elect the 3-member Risk Committee every 6 months, and on major parameters such as the fee switch [6][7]. Ethena has no DAO and no on-chain governance; the filing says "there is no formal threshold or quorum defined yet in ENA voting" [28], although individual Snapshot proposals set their own quorum (5,000,000 for the fee switch; 500,000 for Risk Committee elections) [26]. The Ethena Foundation (Cayman foundation company) acts as "steward ... taking ENA tokenholder votes into account". Contract admin power sits with a 5/11 Dev Multisig 0x3b0aaf6e6fcd4a7ceef8c92c32dfea9e64dc1862 [8][28]. On-chain, owner() of the ENA, USDe and sUSDe contracts is 0xe8dc0fab349ea169283c48ccfd09d797e6db7c94, a verified EthenaTimelockController with getMinDelay() = 86,400 s (24 hours); the Dev Multisig holds its PROPOSER and EXECUTOR roles (hasRole = true), so parameter changes pass through a 24-hour timelock (fact-checker read, 2026-11-10) [32]. Thresholds read on-chain via getThreshold(): Dev 5, sUSDe Payout Fund 3, Reserve Fund 4.

- sENA staking. ENA is deposited into an ERC-4626 vault with an unstaking cooldown [1]. sENA has historically received partner airdrops (Ethereal, Based/HyENA "$BASED claiming live for sENA holders" in April 2026 [21]) and Ethena reward-campaign weighting. It receives no protocol revenue today. The exchange rate of 1.01827 ENA per sENA reflects small cumulative ENA top-ups. OAK Research plans a separate proposal on "sENA value accrual" after the fee switch [17].

- Fee switch (voted, not active). A take on gross protocol revenue is set by the 14-day trailing average USDe supply: 5% at $7.5B, 10% at $10B, 15% at $15B, 20% at $20B. 95% of the net revenue paid to the Foundation from the business lines would buy ENA on the open market; 5% would fund growth [11][17][18]. The take comes pro rata out of the sUSDe, partner-reward and Aave-program allocations [17]. Execution design (venue, contract, burn or hold) has not been published; OAK Research said implementation specifics would follow "over the coming weeks", and on 2026-10-12 a contributor from Aragon (forum user Leuts.eth) suggested, informally, a Euler FeeFlow-style reverse Dutch auction with a price ceiling [17].

- No burn, gas, collateral requirement or ve-locking applies to ENA in the core protocol.

### 4. Utility

- Real today: voting on Risk Committee membership and major parameters (Snapshot, non-binding on the Foundation [28]); staking into sENA for partner airdrops and reward-campaign boosts; collateral or trading asset on exchanges and DeFi (perps on major venues; Coinbase Derivatives ENA futures self-certified for trading on or after 2026-03-02 [28]); restaking (rsENA).

- Not needed for: minting, redeeming or holding USDe/sUSDe/USDtb, paying fees, or backing; product users never touch ENA.

- Prospective: a claim on buybacks once the fee switch activates, plus a possible future sENA reward program [17]. Until then ENA is effectively governance plus expectation. The Foundation's own filing says ENA holders "do not hold any contractual or programmatic right to protocol revenue distributions or treasury assets" [28].

### 5. Why people buy and sell it

#### Demand drivers

- Fee-switch optionality. ENA is a leveraged bet on USDe supply returning to $7.5B+ (it was $14.8B in October 2025). Illustrative buybacks at a 6% protocol APY: $22.5M a year at $7.5B, $60M at $10B, $135M at $15B, $240M at $20B [17]. At the realized 4.6% APY, Blockworks Advisory estimates $17.3M, $46.0M, $103.5M and $184.1M [17].

- Basis-trade beta. USDe supply and yield rise with crypto funding rates and leverage demand. BTC funding averaged 11.0% (2024), 4.9% (2025) and 2.2% YTD to 2026-08-11 [12]. ENA rallied with the re-expansion of the basis trade: hedged positions grew from about 1% of backing in July 2026 to 18.2% on 2026-11-10 [12][31].

- Narratives: tokenized equity and commodity basis (Binance named first equity-perp venue, 2026-09-25) [18]; TradFi distribution (Coinbase, Robinhood Chain, Kraken+, Janus Henderson) [18][19]; "token-equity alignment" through the Master Framework Agreement [11].

- Structured/institutional demand. StablecoinX holds about 20% of supply [11]. Grayscale added ENA to its DeFi Fund at a 13.59% weight on 2026-05-07 [20]. CME-style regulated futures exist via Coinbase Derivatives [28].

#### Supply and sell pressure

- Vesting: ≈189M ENA a month (team, foundation, ecosystem) to ~Mar 2028 (estimate above), ≈$28M a month at $0.1495 (2026-11-10). Scheduled gross unlocks were ≈$512M a year at late-August prices [17].

- Investor overhang: removed for the cohort that was bought out. The remaining investors' tokens were all released on 2026-10-05, so they are now liquid and can be sold at any time [11].

- StablecoinX locked ENA: 25% cliff at the 12-month anniversary of closing, then monthly [28]. Timing not verified.

- Market-maker loans: 46M ENA lent to four market makers on 12-month loan-with-call-option terms [28]. About 2% of supply was spent on exchange listings [28].

- Reflexivity: falling funding rates lower sUSDe yield, which leads to redemptions, lower USDe supply and a weaker fee-switch thesis. ENA fell 35% over 30 days (CoinGecko, 2026-11-10) while USDe supply was flat to slightly up ($4.76B → $4.95B on DefiLlama).

### 6. The protocol/business

What it does. Ethena runs three revenue lines [11]:

- USDe savings. USDe/sUSDe distributed through DeFi (Aave, Morpho, Pendle, Kamino, Jupiter Lend), exchanges (Binance, Bybit, OKX, Deribit, Bitget, Gate, where USDe is margin collateral that pays rewards), wallets (Telegram/TON wallets, Coinbase DeFi earn, Kraken+, Binance Wallet) and Ethena Pay.

- Whitelabel stablecoins. "Stablecoin-as-a-service" built on USDtb: jupUSD (Jupiter), USDm (MegaETH), suiUSDe (Sui).

- "Ethena [X]". Announced on 2026-08-27 as "launching next week". Ethena Pay beta launched on Avalanche on 2026-09-01 (self-custodial money app, rollout to 48 countries, "savings rewards of up to 6%", card) [18]. Whether Ethena [X] is Ethena Pay was not confirmed in the sources reviewed.

Related products: HyENA (USDe-margined perp DEX on Hyperliquid HIP-3, December 2025) [15]; Ethereal, renamed Meridian (USDe-native perp/prediction DEX on Robinhood Chain) [18].

Audience. Traders using USDe as rewarded margin (Binance balances reached $4B within two weeks of integration in 2025; ≈$80M of USDe rewards paid to Binance/Bybit users [15]), DeFi loopers, and retail savers via wallets and exchanges. In the TradFi channel, USDe on Robinhood Chain exceeded $300M (about 40% of dollar supply there) and the Coinbase DeFi earn product exceeded $300M in August 2026 [18]. The product is not offered to EU/EEA residents (sUSDe) or US mint users [28]. TVL on DefiLlama: $5.337B, of which Ethereum is $5.335B and TON $2.4M [29].

