#### Key integrations and partners

Custody/venues: Copper, Ceffu/Binance, Anchorage, Kraken Custody ($41,323 at 2026-10-21 [13]), Coinbase (primary custodian, wallet and perp venue across >$5B, June 2026 [19]), OKX, Bybit. DeFi: Aave v3/v4 (Blockworks Advisory backed an interim v4 allocation of up to $60M, 2026-11-02 [24]), Morpho (USDe is its largest dollar collateral [18]), Pendle, Kamino, Jupiter Lend, Curve. TradFi: Janus Henderson [19], FalconX, Maple, Payward/Kraken lending [18]. Proof of reserves: LlamaRisk, Chainlink, Harris & Trotter [31].

### 7. Revenue and value capture

#### Where revenue comes from

Funding and basis on hedged positions (crypto, and now equities and gold), interest on DeFi and institutional loans, RWA yield (JAAA, STAC; SAFO proposed), stablecoin rewards, USDtb T-bill interest, and mint fees (now mostly zero) [3][18]. Ethena-reported yields (as of 2026-11-04): protocol yield 5.10%, sUSDe 30-day average 5.12%, 90-day average 4.79%, since-inception average 10.23% [31].

#### (a) Gross fees, (b) protocol revenue, (c) token-holder value

| Metric | 24h | 7d | 30d | Annualized / 1y | Source |

| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |

| (a) Gross fees (DefiLlama dailyFees, "staking rewards + yield distribution + mint fees + extra fees") | $703* | $4,473,311 | $17,306,681 | 30d×365/30 ≈ $210.6M; trailing 1y $235.3M; all-time $1.079B | [29] |

| (a) Gross fees, Blockworks Advisory (Ethena governance report) | — | — | Jul $17.6M; Aug $18.4M; Sep $21.3M (USDe fees $15.9/17.2/19.8M; USDtb interest $1.7/1.2/1.5M) | Q3 2026 $57M | [18] |

| (b) Protocol revenue as DefiLlama defines it ("mint fees and staking rewards portion to Reserve Fund") | $703* | $1,420 | $90,656 | trailing 1y $2.02M; all-time $333.0M (mostly 2024 Reserve Fund build-up) | [29] |

| (b) Retained by protocol/Foundation after distributions | Approximately zero. Reserve Fund allocation is 0% and "100% [is] directed to incentive rewards, promotional distributions, and distribution incentives" [5]. Reserve Fund flat at about $62M since early 2025 [18][31]. Mint fees were $8.4M a year (4.7% of gross) in August 2026 and have since gone to 0 bps for USDC/USDT [17][18]. |  |  |  | [5][17] |

| Of gross: paid to sUSDe stakers (on-chain USDe transfers distributor → sUSDe) | 161,816 USDe | 1,125,084 USDe | 4,757,762 USDe | 90d: 14,801,566 USDe (≈$58–60M/yr run-rate on 30d/90d windows) | Etherscan V2 tokentx, my read |

| (c) Reaching ENA holders (buyback, burn, distribution) | $0 | $0 | $0 | $0. Fee switch passed but inactive below $7.5B 14-day average USDe supply; DefiLlama has no holders-revenue series for Ethena ("not found") | [17][29] |

*DefiLlama's 24h figure is not meaningful: Ethena books fees weekly, so the daily series shows a ≈$4.1–4.4M spike every Wednesday or Thursday (e.g. $4,426,895 on 2026-11-05; $4,198,844 on 2026-10-29) and near-zero values on other days.

Cross-check. Blockworks reports the sUSDe share of fee allocation at about 27% in September 2026 [18]. 27% × DefiLlama 30-day fees of $17.31M = $4.67M, compared with $4.76M actually transferred to sUSDe on-chain over the same 30 days, a gap of about 2%. The weekly reward mint (1,132,713.04 USDe on 2026-11-05) divided by 1.2079B staked gives 0.0938% a week, or ≈4.9% simple / 5.0% compounded APY. That matches Ethena's reported 30-day sUSDe APY of 5.12%. The two sources agree. DefiLlama "revenue" only measures mint fees and Reserve Fund top-ups.

Where the gross money goes (allocation of USDe fees, September 2026 [18]): Aave "liquid leverage" incentive program 47%, sUSDe stakers 27%, partner and exchange rewards 27%. In March 2026 the split was 54.6% sUSDe, 27.9% partners, 17.5% Aave [28].

#### Mechanism and contracts

- Most yield accrues off-chain (exchange funding, custodial accounts, loan interest). The Foundation's subsidiary mints USDe weekly from address 0x0 into the StakingRewardsDistributor 0xf2fa332b…c6b439, which calls transferInRewards on sUSDe roughly every 8 hours. The sUSDe Payout Fund multisig is 0x71e4f98e8f20c88112489de3dded4489802a3a87 (3/11) [4][8].

- Partner and exchange rewards and the Aave program are paid by Ethena entities. No single published on-chain fee collector covers them.

- No buyback contract or wallet exists yet. Ethena says accumulated buybacks will be shown on the Transparency dashboard ([app.ethena.fi/dashboards/transparency](https://app.ethena.fi/dashboards/transparency)) [11].

