| $10B | 10% | $60M | $46.0M | ≈$47.5M | ≈2.4% |

| $15B | 15% | $135M | $103.5M | ≈$106.9M | ≈5.3% |

| $20B | 20% | $240M | $184.1M | ≈$190M | ≈9.4% |

Backtest by Blockworks Advisory (705 days, 2024-09-19 to 2026-08-24): with a 14-day trigger, the switch would have run on 118 days and captured $17.04M in total. That is $52.7M a year while active (3.36% buyback yield) but only $8.82M a year averaged over the whole cycle (0.56%). It absorbs about 10% of scheduled gross unlocks while active and under 2% over the cycle [17]. At $7.5B, buybacks of ≈$18M a year compare with my estimate of ≈$339M a year of remaining vesting at $0.1495 (189.06M × 12 × price).

### 8. How to verify on-chain

All reads below were run on 2026-11-10 around 15:32 UTC (block 26,385,426) against https://ethereum-rpc.publicnode.com, unless noted, and re-run by the fact-checker at ~16:10 UTC (block 26,385,626) with the same results except where a second value is shown. Etherscan calls need your own key in $ETHERSCAN_API_KEY.

