As of 2026-11-10. Market data: CoinGecko, 2026-11-10 16:16 UTC. On-chain reads: Ethereum block ~26.39M and World Chain blocks 37,494,701–37,495,919 (2026-11-10 15:37–16:15 UTC). Web search was unavailable, so news comes from primary sources fetched directly (see Verification notes).

### 1. Executive summary

WLD is the ERC-20 token of World, a "proof of human" network. People scan their iris and face at an Orb to get a World ID, and verified users receive WLD. The Cayman Islands World Foundation steers the project and Tools for Humanity (TFH; CEO Alex Blania, chairman Sam Altman) builds most of it. Today no protocol revenue reaches WLD holders. There is no fee switch, buyback, burn or revenue-funded staking. The only on-chain fee stream is World Chain gas, about $400 a day, paid in ETH. The planned value-capture route is "World ID fees", a monthly fee per verified user paid by apps, part of which could be burned. They were described in April 2025 and April 2026, but there is no evidence they are live. The 2026 text also no longer says fees must be paid in WLD. The products are growing: World ID app and World Money launched Sep–Oct 2026; Tinder, Zoom, Okta, Vercel and Docusign integrate it; ~18M people are Orb-verified. The token is in a long drawdown: $0.309, −46.6% over 30 days, −62.4% over a year, ~97% below the $11.74 all-time high. About 2.9M WLD a day still unlocks (≈28% of circulating supply a year), and the Foundation funds itself with over-the-counter (OTC) WLD sales. Conclusion: WLD is an incentive and treasury token whose holders capture no protocol cash flow. The current state is "problems": price and chain activity are falling and Foundation selling continues, despite strong product news. Most important thing to watch: whether World ID fees go live, denominated in WLD and with a burn or holder share. Without that, demand rests on narrative (OpenAI/Altman, AI agents, an ETF) against structural supply.

### 2. What the token is

- Ticker / name: WLD ("Worldcoin"). Launched 2023-07-24. The project was renamed "World" in Oct 2024.

- Contracts (match the [whitepaper table](https://whitepaper.world.org/designing-for-scale) and on-chain reads):

- Ethereum (canonical): 0x163f8C2467924be0ae7B5347228CABF260318753. totalSupply() = 10,000,000,000. owner() = 0x59a0f98345f54bAB245A043488ECE7FCecD7B596 (Safe labeled "World Assets, Ltd. Cold Wallets"). minter() = 0x0.

- World Chain (OP-Stack L2, chainId 480): 0x2cFc85d8E48F8EAB294be644d9E25C3030863003. Supply 817,146,753, backed by 817,647,961 in L1 bridge 0x470458C91978D2d929704489Ad730DC3E3001113.

- Optimism: 0xdC6fF44d5d932Cbd77B52E5612Ba0529DC6226F1. Supply 481.81M, backed by 481,812,030 in L1 gateway 0x99C9fc46f92E8a1c0deC1b1747d010903E884bE1.

- Inflation: none before inflationUnlockTime() = 2163556801 (2038-07-24 04:00 UTC). After that the cap is inflationCapWad 0.1241% per 2,628,000 s, which compounds to 1.5% a year. Using it is a governance choice; the default is 0%. renounceOwnership() reverts.

- Holders: 65,340 on Ethereum, 12,859,723 on World Chain (mostly World App wallets). Source: Blockscout, 2026-11-10 ~16:20 UTC.

