### 3. How it works

- Orb → World ID. An Orb (iris/face scanner) checks that a person is unique and issues a "Proof of Human" credential to a World ID on their phone. Per World, the data is deleted from the Orb and iris codes are secret-shared by multi-party computation. Apps then request zero-knowledge proofs ("unique human", "over 18") without learning identity, and nullifiers stop apps linking a user across services.

- Credentials: Proof of Human (Orb), Proof of Presence (phone liveness check) and Proof of Attributes (NFC passport/ID). Proof of Human has been presented more than 475M times ([World, 2026-10-16](https://world.org/blog/world/world-id-app-identity-wallet-age-of-ai)).

- World ID 4.0 (2026-04-17) is account-based, with key rotation and recovery, an open-source authenticator SDK, and technical enforcement of World ID fees.

- Apps: the World ID app (identity wallet, 150+ countries, 2026-10-16; no Orb required) and World Money (self-custodial stablecoin super app with Bridge accounts, Stripe/Apple Pay on-ramp in the US, Morpho Earn, and Mini Apps such as Kalshi; 150+ countries from 2026-09-17).

- World Chain (Oct 2024) is an OP-Stack L2 in the Optimism Superchain. Gas is paid in ETH, not WLD, and TFH sponsors gas for app users. "Priority Blockspace for Humans" puts verified users ahead of bots.

- Token distribution: free "user tokens": a first amount per credential, then shrinking monthly amounts claimed on World Chain from World Assets contracts. Orb operators are paid in WLD. The Foundation has also paid TFH in WLD since Dec 2025, starting with 93.7M ([source](https://world.org/blog/announcements/building-a-wld-native-economy-across-the-world-protocol)).

- Governance: the Foundation board decides. A DAO can make "recommendations" that the board implements "with best efforts", subject to fiduciary duties. There is no binding on-chain WLD vote.

- Staking / fee switch / buyback / burn: none. In-app WLD yields (advertised "up to 18%", Dec 2025, via Morpho) come from incentives and lending, not protocol revenue. The dead address holds 0.42 WLD.

- Planned: World ID fees. The credential fee goes to the issuer (the Foundation for Orb credentials); the protocol fee goes to a protocol wallet. Apps pre-fund wallets and pay a monthly fee per active verified user. Protocol fees "may" be partly burned, as configured by the Foundation ([2026-04-16](https://world.org/blog/announcements/world-id-fees-the-revenue-potential-from-world-id)).

### 4. Utility

| Use | Real today? | Comment |

| --- | --- | --- |

| Incentive to verify (Orb or passport) | Yes | The main live function. It is shrinking: on-chain claims are ~13.9k WLD a day |

| Payments in World Money | Optional | Stablecoins are the default balance |

| Collateral / yield (Morpho, WLD Vault) | Yes, small | ~37M WLD in Morpho, ~46M in WLD Vault |

| Gas on World Chain | No | Gas is paid in ETH |

| App fees for World ID | Not yet | Not live. The 2025 design said WLD; the 2026 text says "the asset used to settle fees" |

| Governance | Nominal | The Foundation board decides |

| Required to use World ID | No | Users and apps need no WLD |

Bottom line: WLD is an incentive and treasury token today. The "real utility" thesis depends on future World ID fees.

### 5. Why people buy and sell it

#### Demand

- OpenAI/Altman and AI proxy. On 2026-01-28 WLD rose 40% to $0.63 after Forbes reported that OpenAI plans a bot-free social network ([Cointelegraph](https://cointelegraph.com/news/worldcoin-token-spike-report-openai-build-biometric-x-rival)). In June 2026 it topped $0.60 after Maelstrom called it an "AI IPO" proxy, then fell back to $0.40 when Arthur Hayes sold ([Cointelegraph](https://cointelegraph.com/news/arthur-hayes-offloads-wld-days-after-maelstrom-touted-it-as-an-ai-ipo-play)).

- "Proof of Human for the agentic web": Okta, Vercel, Browserbase, Exa, Coinbase AgentKit (Mar 2026), Zoom, Docusign, Tinder US (Jul 2026).

- Institutional wrappers: the Grayscale Worldcoin ETF (GWLD, Nasdaq) S-1 was filed 2026-07-20; EDGAR shows no later filing as of 2026-11-10. Eightco holds ~302M WLD.

- Korean retail and derivatives: Bithumb (6.7%) and Upbit (4.3%) carry ≈11% of spot volume across the top 100 CoinGecko tickers. Perp open interest is $275.7M across 75 markets; 24h perp volume is $597M versus $129.3M spot (CoinGecko, 2026-11-10 ~16:20 UTC).

- Strategic buyers: a16z and Bain Capital Crypto bought $135M in May 2025 (the ≈$1.13 price was not re-verified). A Pantera-led group bought $52.5M of locked WLD in Jul 2026 with Bain Capital Crypto, Eightco, Selini and Susquehanna Crypto (12-month lockup).

#### Supply / sell pressure

- Unlocks: ~2.9M WLD a day until mid-2028, then ~1.6M a day (community only).

- Foundation OTC sales. March 2026: World Assets sold $65M to four counterparties at ≈$0.27 (~239M WLD). $25M was locked for 6 months; the first tranche settled 2026-03-20 ([Cointelegraph](https://cointelegraph.com/news/sam-altman-world-wld-sale-65m-token-lows)). On-chain, the cold wallet sent 230M to ops Safe 0xe797…61a3 on 2026-03-18. On 2026-07-24, tx 0xb7ea51b4… moved 217.4M: 157.4M to 12 addresses in $-tranche sizes at $0.27 (e.g. 18,518,518 ≈ $5M), plus 60M to the ops Safe. On 2026-09-28, tx 0x44246085… moved 214.7M: 124.7M to 6 addresses and 90M to the ops Safe. The ops Safe then sent 105M to Safe 0x3857…269e on 2026-09-30. Mapping these transfers to deals is inference.

- Releases to treasury from the first community contract 0x1770…C296 (now empty): 1,395,998,898 WLD on 2025-12-24 (tx 0x2818f5d5…, which also sent 60M out to 0xf0007b56…) and 674.6M on 2026-08-11 (0x7ff8e9dc…).

- WLD payments to TFH, Orb operators and grantees, who have fiat costs. User-token selling is now small.

### 6. The protocol / business

- What it does: sells "Proof of Human", a privacy-preserving way for platforms to know a user is a unique person. Product lines: World ID protocol and app, World Money, World Chain. Enterprise products: World ID for Zoom, World ID for banking and finance (Money20/20, 2026-10-16; design partners Bain Capital, OpenExchange, Outtake, Pantera Capital, VanEck), Concert Kit (ticketing), AgentKit (AI agents).

- Strategy: World entered "Phase 3" of its Simple Plan on 2026-07-24: bring Proof of Human to consumer platforms, enterprises and AI agents ([source](https://world.org/blog/announcements/world-year-three)).

- Audience: ~18M Orb-verified people in 160 countries. That was 12M in Apr 2025, "nearly 18M" in Apr 2026 and "more than 18M" in Oct 2026, so growth has slowed. There were 26M app accounts in Apr 2025 (no newer figure). US launch 2025-05-01 targeted 7,500 Orbs in 12 months. Flagships in Munich (May 2026) and London (Jul 2026); Orbs at the NYSE. Historically strong in Latin America (Argentina), Southeast Asia, Japan, Korea, Portugal and Germany, mostly among emerging-market retail users. The enterprise push targets US/EU platforms.

