### 7. Revenue and value capture

| Layer | 24h | 7d | 30d | 1y | Source / note |

| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |

| (a) Gross fees: World Chain gas (ETH) | $397 (2026-11-09); on-chain 0.2073 ETH ≈ $417 | $3,112; on-chain 1.4812 ETH ≈ $2,979 | $17,345 | $205,634 | DefiLlama, cross-checked with fee-vault balance deltas (Section 8.5); agree within ~5% |

| (a') World ID fees from apps | $0 | $0 | $0 | $0 | Not live; no fee contract or announcement found as of 2026-11-10 |

| (b) Protocol revenue | Sequencer margin = gas − batcher L1 posting costs − Optimism Superchain share, so it is at most ≈$0.4k a day (net not computed). DefiLlama has no dailyRevenue series ("not found", 2026-11-10). All three fee vaults pay RECIPIENT() = 0xB2aa0C2C4fD6BFCBF699d4c787CD6Cc0dC461a9d (unlabeled EOA, presumably the chain operator). TFH's app and Orb revenue is undisclosed. |  |  |  | Fee vaults 0x42…11/19/1a |

| (c) To WLD holders | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | No mechanism exists; DefiLlama has no dailyHoldersRevenue |

Mechanism: gas accrues in ETH in SequencerFeeVault 0x4200…0011, BaseFeeVault 0x4200…0019 and L1FeeVault 0x4200…001a. None of it is converted to WLD.

Stated monetization plan:

- [2025-04-30](https://world.org/blog/announcements/introducing-world-id-fees): fees "payable in WLD", charged to apps rather than users. Credential fee plus protocol fee; apps pre-fund wallets. The Foundation could "even decide to burn a share". A pilot was promised for Q3 2025; no results are public.

- [2026-04-16](https://world.org/blog/announcements/world-id-fees-the-revenue-potential-from-world-id): World ID 4.0 makes fees enforceable. Worked example: $5 a year ($0.40 a month) per active verified user. Protocol fees "may burn a share". The fee asset is now "the asset used to settle fees on the protocol", not WLD.

- Illustration, not a forecast: 18M × $5 = $90M a year if every verified human were active in a paying app. That is ≈7.8% of the $1.16B market cap. Only an undefined protocol-fee/burn share would reach WLD.

