### 11. Current problems and risks

- No value accrual. Holders receive $0. On-chain revenue is ~$0.2M a year of ETH gas, against a $3.1B FDV. World ID fees are ~14 months past the end of Q3 2025, when a pilot was promised. The 2026 design no longer commits to WLD.

- Supply overhang. ~2.9M WLD a day unlocks (≈28% of circulating a year). 175M community WLD is releasable now. The treasury holds 1.18B unlocked WLD. The Foundation keeps selling at discounts ($0.27 in March, and by tranche math in July and September). July 2026 locked buyers unlock ~2027-07-24.

- Product decoupled from token. The World ID app needs no Orb, World Money defaults to stablecoins, gas is ETH, and enterprise customers never touch WLD.

- Slowing growth. Verified users are flat at ~18M since Apr 2026. TVL is −67% from its peak. Stablecoins fell $28.2M→$16.2M year on year. Daily transactions fell ~32% in early Nov.

- Regulatory and privacy: Thailand (raid, 1.2M-scan deletion order), plus Indonesia, Germany, Kenya, Brazil, Spain and Portugal. WLD is unavailable to New York residents.

- Centralization: a 4-person board, a Foundation-owned contract (it can set a minter after 2038), Foundation-set user-token amounts, and an advisory-only DAO.

- Reflexive trading: perp open interest is $276M against a ~$1.16B market cap, and perp volume is ~4.6x spot (2026-11-10). The price is headline-driven (OpenAI, Hayes/Maelstrom).

- Bull case: AI agents and deepfakes make proof of human mandatory; World has an 18M-person biometric network and blue-chip integrations; an ETF and treasury companies widen access; and a fee switch with burns would turn usage into token demand.

