### Verification notes

An independent fact-check ran on 2026-11-10, 16:00–16:30 UTC. It re-queried chain state, APIs and the linked pages rather than reusing the draft.

#### Re-checked and confirmed

- Ethereum reads. All match the doc: totalSupply, the cold-wallet balance, owner, minter, the inflation parameters (1.50% a year compounded) and the dead-address balance.

- VestingWallets and bridges. Balances, start dates, durations and the beneficiary (cold wallet) of the three community VestingWallets match. So do the bridge balances and World Chain supply. The addresses match the whitepaper and CoinGecko's platform list.

- DefiLlama. Fees, TVL, stablecoins, DEX volume and all-app fees reproduced exactly. My own fee-vault deltas match DefiLlama within ~5%.

- Treasury transfers. The Etherscan V2 transactions (2026-03-18, 07-24, 08-11, 09-28, 09-30) were confirmed, as were both locked-sale VestingWallets.

- Official pages. These confirm the Foundation board and the World Assets role, TFH founders and staff count, the unlock-rate post, both fee posts, the 18M+ verified users and 475M presentations, World Money, Phase 3, the banking partners and the Zoom listing.

- News. Cointelegraph confirms the $65M sale, the $52.5M sale (12-month lock), the Grayscale S-1 (filed Monday 2026-07-20), the OpenAI spike to $0.63, the Hayes episode and the Thailand order. EDGAR shows a single S-1 for Grayscale and confirms Eightco's 301,971,219 and ~302M WLD.

- Links and format. All 44 links in the draft returned HTTP 200. All 13 sections are present in order, in English, with no API keys and no predictions.

#### Corrected

- The 2025-12-24 release was 1,396.0M WLD, not 1,456.0M. 1,456.0M is the transaction total, which includes a 60M outflow.

- The Section 8.4 eth_getLogs example used a 101-block range, which the RPC rejects. Fixed to 0x23c1fac.

- The competitor table had a stale WLD market cap ($1.14B / FDV $3.05B) that contradicted the supply table. Price, market cap, FDV, 30d/1y change, holders, open interest ($281.7M → $275.7M), perp and spot volume, and the Korean exchange share are all refreshed to 16:16–16:21 UTC.

- The "Oct average" of World Chain transactions covered only Oct 10–31. The decline also started Oct 27–28 (680–717k), not Oct 31, which was 538.5k.

- The World ID fee delay is "~14 months" past the end of Q3 2025, not "~18 months".

- "Sequencer margin ≈ gas" was wrong. The margin is at most gas. DefiLlama has no revenue series. The fee-vault recipient is now named.

- Added facts: the likely TFH custody wallet 0x1296…0569 (inference); the 2026-10-28 locked-sale VestingWallet funding; the peaq date (2026-09-30); 10B is not a hard cap after 2038; an explicit conclusion in the summary; and both dates (10-16 and 10-18) for the October posts.

- Prose was condensed to fit the Google Docs upload limit. No numbers were removed.

#### Not independently verified

- The ≈$1.13 price of the May 2025 a16z/Bain purchase, the regulatory country list, the flagship store dates and the X handles. The ~5.85B unlocked supply is a model estimate; my recomputation gives ≈5.83B.

- Mapping treasury transfers to specific OTC deals is inference.

- Web search was unavailable to both the author and the checker. News after mid-October comes from the world.org blog (latest post 2026-11-02) and the Cointelegraph RSS feed (latest item 2026-10-19), so items reported only on X may be missing. That includes a possible World ID fee launch, though none was found.
